<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Alternative/bf8747c0-87fd-412b-a4a1-2134188018d5> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Alternative/bf8747c0-87fd-412b-a4a1-2134188018d5> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Retaining the prior TripleSet/TripleMap representation would keep indexed-graph-match/for-each/contains/subjects/objects returning triples straight from the index without any record-new reconstruction, but at ~3x the per-key memory (216 vs 72 bytes) that this commit's new comment identifies as the cost being paid down. Evidence: src/index.slop's new comment block quantifying the 72-vs-216-byte difference, and the diff reintroducing `(record-new Triple ...)` at every former direct-push site (indexed-graph-match, indexed-graph-for-each)." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Alternative/bf8747c0-87fd-412b-a4a1-2134188018d5> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
