<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Alternative/fddbc9fe-3665-4be9-bc25-4e83e633bec6> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Alternative/fddbc9fe-3665-4be9-bc25-4e83e633bec6> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-09-30T04:13:49.001186Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Alternative/fddbc9fe-3665-4be9-bc25-4e83e633bec6> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "mmap the input file instead of file-read-all into the arena: measured on GO as fread+touch 6.8 ms vs mmap+touch 2.5 ms (about 1.5% of the 310 ms parse) with no RSS gain since file-backed pages count toward resident size; below the 10% adoption bar, and unsafe for the non-streaming parse whose Graph would outlive the mapping." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/0b81e39e-f532-49c3-a7bb-cde73f43c7bd> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/0b81e39e-f532-49c3-a7bb-cde73f43c7bd> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Callback-based indexed-graph-for-each avoids result-list allocation" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/0b81e39e-f532-49c3-a7bb-cde73f43c7bd> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/0b81e39e-f532-49c3-a7bb-cde73f43c7bd> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "indexed-graph-for-each is a new public function that takes a callback (Fn (Triple) Unit) and invokes it once per matching triple, instead of building and returning a List Triple like indexed-graph-match. It re-implements the same per-field subject/predicate/object equality filtering over g.triples that indexed-graph-match now uses (introduced in this same commit), but calls the callback directly rather than pushing into a result list — avoiding the List allocation itself, on top of the Triple-allocation avoidance already made in indexed-graph-match. Marked @pure. Evidence: src/index.slop, new (fn indexed-graph-for-each ((in g IndexedGraph) (in subj (Option Term)) (in pred (Option Term)) (in obj (Option Term)) (callback (Fn (Triple) Unit))) ...), @intent \"Call callback for each matching triple - zero allocation\", :c-name \"rdf_indexed_graph_for_each\"." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/0b81e39e-f532-49c3-a7bb-cde73f43c7bd> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/0b81e39e-f532-49c3-a7bb-cde73f43c7bd> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-02-04T23:47:59Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/0b81e39e-f532-49c3-a7bb-cde73f43c7bd> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Callback-based indexed-graph-for-each avoids result-list allocation" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/0b81e39e-f532-49c3-a7bb-cde73f43c7bd> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#resultsIn> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/b12354f4-127d-41bb-ab96-05888d2d11ff> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/0b81e39e-f532-49c3-a7bb-cde73f43c7bd> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#weighs> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Alternative/9d221953-0f9c-492a-85cc-cb9bb8f71dba> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/0fea10c1-0a41-4526-978e-bf83479a4e27> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/0fea10c1-0a41-4526-978e-bf83479a4e27> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Executable meteorites benchmark for TTL parser" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/0fea10c1-0a41-4526-978e-bf83479a4e27> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/0fea10c1-0a41-4526-978e-bf83479a4e27> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Adds bench/ as a standalone Slop sub-project (bench/slop.toml — entry parse-meteorites.slop, building ../build/parse_meteorites against ../src and ../src/parse) whose main() parses the new test_data/meteorites.ttl fixture (a ~710,000-line real-world Turtle graph) inside a 64MB arena and prints the resulting graph size — giving the TTL parser's ongoing performance work an executable, real-data benchmark instead of only unit tests. Evidence: commit 3442934 (\"performance tweaks\"), new files bench/parse-meteorites.slop, bench/slop.toml, and test_data/meteorites.ttl." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/0fea10c1-0a41-4526-978e-bf83479a4e27> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/0fea10c1-0a41-4526-978e-bf83479a4e27> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-06-29T14:07:04Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/0fea10c1-0a41-4526-978e-bf83479a4e27> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Executable meteorites benchmark for TTL parser" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/1afcbec8-fd6c-4396-838a-321b5c6e58fa> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/1afcbec8-fd6c-4396-838a-321b5c6e58fa> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Linear-scan filtering replaces index dispatch in indexed-graph-match" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/1afcbec8-fd6c-4396-838a-321b5c6e58fa> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/1afcbec8-fd6c-4396-838a-321b5c6e58fa> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "indexed-graph-match no longer consults the SPO/PSO/OSP indexes for any binding pattern; it always performs a full linear scan of g.triples, checking subject/predicate/object equality per triple via term-eq and pushing the existing triple reference (not a freshly allocated one via make-triple) into the result list when all bound fields match. This applies uniformly regardless of which of subject/predicate/object are bound — previously, a bound subject used the SPO index, a bound predicate (with unbound subject) used PSO, a bound object (with both others unbound) used OSP, and only the fully-unbound case fell back to scanning triples. The three index maps (SPO/PSO/OSP) are still built and maintained by indexed-graph-add, and indexed-graph-contains/indexed-graph-subjects/indexed-graph-objects are unchanged in this diff and presumably still read from them — only indexed-graph-match's dispatch was retired. The pre-existing @assume correctness axioms bridging match's result to g.triples (from the \"IndexedGraph query correctness axioms\" constraint) are unchanged by this diff and are now trivially satisfied by construction rather than needing to bridge from index structure. Evidence: src/index.slop, commit d2e13ff." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/1afcbec8-fd6c-4396-838a-321b5c6e58fa> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "superseded" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/1afcbec8-fd6c-4396-838a-321b5c6e58fa> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasRationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/58d5f796-1949-4984-b98b-56a6db65bd42> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/1afcbec8-fd6c-4396-838a-321b5c6e58fa> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-02-04T23:47:59Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
