<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/1c874317-232d-42a6-a2e9-7f650cece2f8> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Streaming TTL file serializer via fwrite FFI" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/1c874317-232d-42a6-a2e9-7f650cece2f8> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/1c874317-232d-42a6-a2e9-7f650cece2f8> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "serialize-ttl-stream is a new public function that writes a graph directly to an open FILE* via a new `(ffi \"stdio.h\" (fwrite ...))` binding and an emit-str helper, instead of building the entire output as one arena-allocated string via serialize-ttl-string (as serialize-ttl-file does) and writing it out in a single file-write-line call. It wraps each triple's subject/predicate/object rendering in a fresh `(with-arena 4096 ...)` block inside its for-each loop and writes each piece out immediately via emit-str/fwrite, so arena usage is bounded per-triple instead of accumulating every serialized string fragment for the whole graph in one arena for the life of the call. Evidence: src/serialize/serialize-ttl.slop's new `(ffi \"stdio.h\" (fwrite ((buf (Ptr Void)) (size U64) (count U64) (file (Ptr Void))) U64))` import, the new `emit-str` and `serialize-ttl-stream` functions (the latter under the header comment \"Streaming serializer — O(n) arena usage\"), and the `(with-arena 4096 ...)` wrapping each triple's rendering." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/1c874317-232d-42a6-a2e9-7f650cece2f8> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/1c874317-232d-42a6-a2e9-7f650cece2f8> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-02-07T03:15:11Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
