<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/2e773a00-4289-4015-b146-3c0ab5e9c031> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "needs-escaping fast path for TTL string escaping" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/2e773a00-4289-4015-b146-3c0ab5e9c031> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/2e773a00-4289-4015-b146-3c0ab5e9c031> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "escape-string now calls a new needs-escaping(s) pre-check and returns the input string s unchanged when it contains none of the six escape-triggering characters (newline=10, CR=13, tab=9, backslash=92, double-quote=34), skipping the character-by-character loop that previously ran unconditionally, calling string-concat once per character, for every serialized string regardless of content. Evidence: src/serialize/serialize-ttl.slop's new `(fn needs-escaping ...)` under `(@intent \"Check if string contains characters that need Turtle escaping\")`; escape-string's body changed from an unconditional `(let ((len ...) (mut result \"\"))` per-character while-loop to `(if (not (needs-escaping s)) s (let (...) ...))` wrapping that same loop." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/2e773a00-4289-4015-b146-3c0ab5e9c031> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/2e773a00-4289-4015-b146-3c0ab5e9c031> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-02-07T03:15:11Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/2e773a00-4289-4015-b146-3c0ab5e9c031> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "needs-escaping fast path for TTL string escaping" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
