<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/3f1b05e9-bcf8-4f13-977c-fbcee93d2b74> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "String-returning IRI/prefixed-name parsers for datatype literals" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/3f1b05e9-bcf8-4f13-977c-fbcee93d2b74> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/3f1b05e9-bcf8-4f13-977c-fbcee93d2b74> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "parse-iri-ref-string and parse-prefixed-name-string are new functions in src/parse/ttl.slop that parse an IRI reference / prefixed name and return just the resulting String value (via a new StringResult record and a one-line some-string wrapper), instead of routing through parse-iri-ref/parse-prefixed-name which build a full Term and require the caller to match on the term-iri variant to pull the string back out. parse-literal's numeric-datatype branch (the `<...>` and prefixed-name cases following `^^`) is rewritten to call these new string-returning functions directly, dropping the previous `(match (. ir term) ((term-iri iri-val) ...) (_ (error ...)))` dispatch entirely — including its defensive-but-unreachable \"Expected IRI for datatype\" error arm, since parse-iri-ref/parse-prefixed-name always produce a term-iri in this position. Evidence: commit 3442934 (\"performance tweaks\"), src/parse/ttl.slop's new parse-iri-ref-string/parse-prefixed-name-string/some-string functions and the diff replacing the two `(let ((ir (? (parse-iri-ref arena dt-ctx)))) (match (. ir term) ...))`-style blocks in parse-literal's datatype branch." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/3f1b05e9-bcf8-4f13-977c-fbcee93d2b74> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/3f1b05e9-bcf8-4f13-977c-fbcee93d2b74> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-06-29T14:07:04Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/3f1b05e9-bcf8-4f13-977c-fbcee93d2b74> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "String-returning IRI/prefixed-name parsers for datatype literals" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/3f1b05e9-bcf8-4f13-977c-fbcee93d2b74> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#resultsIn> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/eac949da-b306-4484-ac9e-8754449cd37c> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/3f1b05e9-bcf8-4f13-977c-fbcee93d2b74> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#weighs> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Alternative/4842b1a6-565a-4b15-b3ba-b9a0c04a1cc0> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/4259ec3f-7488-4b1c-a390-0e25f7ad6c60> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/4259ec3f-7488-4b1c-a390-0e25f7ad6c60> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Per-statement scratch arena for streaming TTL parse" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/4259ec3f-7488-4b1c-a390-0e25f7ad6c60> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/4259ec3f-7488-4b1c-a390-0e25f7ad6c60> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "parse-ttl-string-for-each-triple parses every top-level triple statement in a 1 MiB scratch arena (explicit arena-new / slop_arena_reset via c-inline / arena-free) and resets it once that statement's triples have been delivered; directives, the prefix map, the base IRI and the blank-label table stay in the caller's long-lived arena. Memory is therefore bounded by the largest statement, not the document.\n\nSupporting changes in src/parse/ttl.slop:\n- prefixed names: prefix scanned without allocating and looked up through a zero-copy view of the input; the IRI is built with one allocation (concat-base-slice), down from three (prefix, local, concat);\n- string literals: scan-string-body finds the end and counts/validates escapes, then decode-string-body makes one substring (no escapes) or one decoded buffer, replacing O(n^2) string-push-char loops;\n- blank labels in a Map (see \"Blank label map for _:label node identity\");\n- nested [ ], collection, triple-term and annotation triples stay as extra-triples lists, now allocated in scratch;\n- errors free scratch explicitly and use match rather than ?, because ? returns without freeing open arenas.\n\nWhy: HOWL streams GO/EL-GALEN/OBI through this entry point; everything accumulated in the one arena until the parse returned (451/481/209 MiB peak with a no-op callback).\n\nEvidence (bench/parse-stream.slop, no-op callback, median of 7, 2026-09-29): GO 76 MB 392->310 ms, 451->74 MiB; EL-GALEN 7.1 MB 79->46 ms, 481->9.3 MiB; OBI 5 MB 41->25 ms, 209->7.0 MiB. The bench's order-sensitive hash over every term (text, kind, blank id) is identical before and after on all three plus meteorites.ttl. In HOWL (GO .ttl, --timings, median of 7): parse_ms 674->592, parse_mb 851->474; all goldens (including the -I import golden with offset _:b2), golden-asan and determinism unchanged. Builds on \"Callback-based streaming hook for TTL parsing\" (https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/c09ecf18-b7cd-42f9-b4ba-419e498f61ed)." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/4259ec3f-7488-4b1c-a390-0e25f7ad6c60> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
