<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/57b948d3-ce19-4e6e-8951-59ad3501a1d0> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/57b948d3-ce19-4e6e-8951-59ad3501a1d0> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Language tag body lexed with is-pn-chars, not is-pn-chars-base" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/57b948d3-ce19-4e6e-8951-59ad3501a1d0> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/57b948d3-ce19-4e6e-8951-59ad3501a1d0> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "parse-literal's `@`-language-tag branch in src/parse/ttl.slop now scans the tag body with `is-pn-chars` instead of `is-pn-chars-base`, so the lexer accepts letters, digits, `_` (95), and `-` (45) in a language tag rather than letters alone. Rationale: `is-pn-chars-base` is defined as `is-alpha` only (src/parse/ttl.slop:1256-1263), so it rejected any language tag whose subtags contain digits — e.g. BCP47 region/variant subtags like \"en-419\" or \"de-DE-1996\" — since after the leading letters the scan would stop at the first digit. `is-pn-chars` adds digit/`_`/`-` on top of `is-pn-chars-base` (src/parse/ttl.slop:1273), so hyphenated multi-subtag language tags now parse correctly. Evidence: commit 14fb02d50d (\"more updates to support snarl\"), src/parse/ttl.slop hunk changing `(let ((lang-result (parse-while arena s2 is-pn-chars-base)))` to `(let ((lang-result (parse-while arena s2 is-pn-chars)))`." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/57b948d3-ce19-4e6e-8951-59ad3501a1d0> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/57b948d3-ce19-4e6e-8951-59ad3501a1d0> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-02-13T03:03:21Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/57b948d3-ce19-4e6e-8951-59ad3501a1d0> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Language tag body lexed with is-pn-chars, not is-pn-chars-base" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/57b948d3-ce19-4e6e-8951-59ad3501a1d0> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#resultsIn> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/a57c5f15-39b7-4b97-8096-249703fe6755> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/58d69b61-cacd-42a4-bf3c-5b616d359864> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/58d69b61-cacd-42a4-bf3c-5b616d359864> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Blank label binding list for `_:label` node identity" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/58d69b61-cacd-42a4-bf3c-5b616d359864> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/58d69b61-cacd-42a4-bf3c-5b616d359864> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "TtlParseContext now tracks a `blank-labels (List BlankLabelBinding)` list of label->id bindings, and parse-blank-node's `_:label` branch looks up the label via the new `blank-label-lookup` before deciding what to do: if the label was already seen, it reuses the existing blank node id; only if the label is new does it call `context-gen-blank-id` and push a fresh `BlankLabelBinding` (label, id) onto the list. Previously every `_:label` occurrence called `context-gen-blank-id` unconditionally, so `_:x` appearing twice in one document produced two distinct blank nodes instead of one.\n\nWhy: Turtle/RDF blank node label semantics require that repeated occurrences of the same `_:label` within a single document denote the SAME blank node — the prior unconditional-generate behavior silently violated that identity requirement, splitting one intended blank node into N unrelated ones.\n\nEvidence: commit f41a7abaae (\"parser fixes\"), src/parse/ttl.slop — new `(type BlankLabelBinding (record (label String) (id (Int 0 ..))))`, new `blank-label-lookup` function, and the rewritten `_:label` branch of parse-blank-node's inner `match` (comment changed from \"_:label syntax\" to \"_:label syntax — reuse same blank node ID for same label\")." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/58d69b61-cacd-42a4-bf3c-5b616d359864> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "superseded" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/58d69b61-cacd-42a4-bf3c-5b616d359864> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-02-12T06:37:10Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/58d69b61-cacd-42a4-bf3c-5b616d359864> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Blank label binding list for `_:label` node identity" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/58d69b61-cacd-42a4-bf3c-5b616d359864> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#isSupersededBy> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/52e7f143-3c47-4dfd-b7cb-4fce4e305c31> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/58d69b61-cacd-42a4-bf3c-5b616d359864> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#resultsIn> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/f40405f6-c310-4afd-a6f7-32547e566690> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/58d69b61-cacd-42a4-bf3c-5b616d359864> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#yieldsLesson> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/8ef105c2-45fa-4729-912b-29a9ab655270> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/5bdf80d4-cb1f-45ad-8e95-98f4356fee47> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/5bdf80d4-cb1f-45ad-8e95-98f4356fee47> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Triple-valued leaves in TripleIndex (TripleSet/TripleMap)" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/5bdf80d4-cb1f-45ad-8e95-98f4356fee47> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/5bdf80d4-cb1f-45ad-8e95-98f4356fee47> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "The SPO/PSO/OSP index maps in TripleIndex now store the full Triple at their second-level leaves instead of just the third field's bare Term. `TermMap (Map Term (Set Term))` / `TermIndex (Map Term TermMap)` are replaced by `TripleSet (Set Triple)` / `TripleMap (Map Term TripleSet)`, and TripleIndex's spo/pso/osp fields are retyped to `(Map Term TripleMap)`. indexed-graph-add now does `(set-put triple-set t)` at all three index leaves (previously `(set-put obj-set o)` for spo/pso and `(set-put pred-set p)` for osp), pushing the identical `t` reference already stored in g.triples, so any index lookup returns that same reference rather than one reconstructed via make-triple. indexed-graph-contains, indexed-graph-subjects, and indexed-graph-objects were all rewritten to match: contains now does `(set-has triple-set t)` on the whole triple instead of `(set-has obj-set o)`; subjects scans each subject's triple-set for a member whose triple-predicate matches, instead of checking `(set-has pred-set pred)`; objects extracts `(triple-object t)` from each stored triple instead of iterating a bare object-set. Evidence: src/index.slop, commit 730e3e4 (\"performance improvements\")." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/5bdf80d4-cb1f-45ad-8e95-98f4356fee47> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "superseded" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/5bdf80d4-cb1f-45ad-8e95-98f4356fee47> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-02-05T18:00:36Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
