<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/5bdf80d4-cb1f-45ad-8e95-98f4356fee47> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#weighs> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Alternative/ad96a489-95e6-4d32-b1ef-a6fe70d48dae> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/5d67c78c-0166-4c2b-b412-12a8d839fee0> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/5d67c78c-0166-4c2b-b412-12a8d839fee0> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Redundant SPO/PSO/OSP indexes for triple lookup" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/5d67c78c-0166-4c2b-b412-12a8d839fee0> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/5d67c78c-0166-4c2b-b412-12a8d839fee0> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "IndexedGraph maintains three parallel index maps — SPO (subject→predicate→objects), PSO (predicate→subject→objects), OSP (object→subject→predicates) — each a two-level map-of-map terminating in a `Set Term`, with every added triple duplicated into all three. `indexed-graph-match` dispatches to whichever index matches the bound components (subject bound → SPO, else predicate bound → PSO, else object bound → OSP) and only falls back to returning the raw `triples` list when nothing is bound. Evidence: src/index.slop — `indexed-graph-add`'s `(let ((s ...) (p ...) (o ...)) ...)` block updates all three maps per triple; `indexed-graph-match`'s nested `match subj/pred/obj` dispatch; `indexed-graph-contains`, `indexed-graph-subjects`, `indexed-graph-objects` each read from a single index rather than scanning `triples`." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/5d67c78c-0166-4c2b-b412-12a8d839fee0> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "superseded" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/5d67c78c-0166-4c2b-b412-12a8d839fee0> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-01-23T07:28:17Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/5d67c78c-0166-4c2b-b412-12a8d839fee0> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Redundant SPO/PSO/OSP indexes for triple lookup" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/5d67c78c-0166-4c2b-b412-12a8d839fee0> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#resultsIn> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/283aee93-f1b4-4bd0-afe5-4eef9ddb1575> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/5d67c78c-0166-4c2b-b412-12a8d839fee0> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#resultsIn> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/7353d1fc-af26-44f2-875f-44c37d14bf6c> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/5d67c78c-0166-4c2b-b412-12a8d839fee0> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#weighs> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Alternative/235bbe3e-88e3-41dc-b7f8-2d3ea7dbf657> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/787f1ae4-9ca5-4758-8157-8f3763d5d7e0> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/787f1ae4-9ca5-4758-8157-8f3763d5d7e0> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Callback-assume axioms for indexed-graph-for-each" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/787f1ae4-9ca5-4758-8157-8f3763d5d7e0> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/787f1ae4-9ca5-4758-8157-8f3763d5d7e0> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "indexed-graph-for-each's callback argument is now covered by four `@callback-assume` contract clauses: one trusted axiom that every triple passed to callback is contained in the graph (`(indexed-graph-contains g $callback-arg)`), and three more — each an `(implies (!= X (none)) (term-eq (triple-X $callback-arg) (unwrap X)))` — asserting that when subj/pred/obj is bound, every callback-delivered triple matches that field. These are declared as `@callback-assume`, the callback-argument analog of the `@assume` axioms already bridging indexed-graph-match/indexed-graph-contains's SPO/PSO/OSP index dispatch back to ground-truth triples-list semantics (per the existing \"IndexedGraph query correctness axioms\" constraint) — trusted, not runtime-proven, assumptions about what values reach a higher-order callback rather than about a function's return value. Evidence: src/index.slop, the four new `(@callback-assume callback ...)` lines inserted directly after indexed-graph-for-each's existing `@pre (>= (. g size) 0)` and before its `(match subj ...)` index-dispatch body, under the new comments \"Callback only receives triples from the graph\" and \"Callback receives triples matching subject/predicate/object filter\"." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/787f1ae4-9ca5-4758-8157-8f3763d5d7e0> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/787f1ae4-9ca5-4758-8157-8f3763d5d7e0> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-02-08T21:36:29Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/787f1ae4-9ca5-4758-8157-8f3763d5d7e0> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Callback-assume axioms for indexed-graph-for-each" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/787f1ae4-9ca5-4758-8157-8f3763d5d7e0> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#isConstrainedBy> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/cc56ed06-7a6b-4ef4-8d5a-1feb56b986e5> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/787f1ae4-9ca5-4758-8157-8f3763d5d7e0> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#resultsIn> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/0a1a482f-6838-4f0e-b9d7-ec7074407da5> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/7c9de607-eccf-43da-802e-14a58d774219> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/7c9de607-eccf-43da-802e-14a58d774219> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "IndexedGraph twin for RDF list traversal" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/7c9de607-eccf-43da-802e-14a58d774219> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/7c9de607-eccf-43da-802e-14a58d774219> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "rdf-list-elements-indexed duplicates rdf-list-elements's rdf:first/rdf:rest traversal loop but operates over IndexedGraph via indexed-graph-match instead of Graph via graph-match, so callers already holding an IndexedGraph can extract list elements using the indexed SPO/PSO/OSP lookups from the earlier indexing decision rather than falling back to a plain-Graph linear scan. Evidence: src/list.slop — the new function imports (index IndexedGraph indexed-graph-match) and, inside a while (not (term-eq current nil-term)) loop, calls indexed-graph-match arena g (some current) (some first-pred|rest-pred) no-obj at each step, mirroring rdf-list-elements's control flow one-for-one (same contract style, same look-up-first-then-look-up-rest structure) but against the indexed API introduced by the \"Redundant SPO/PSO/OSP indexes for triple lookup\" decision (https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/5d67c78c-0166-4c2b-b412-12a8d839fee0)." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/7c9de607-eccf-43da-802e-14a58d774219> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/7c9de607-eccf-43da-802e-14a58d774219> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-01-24T17:26:24Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/7c9de607-eccf-43da-802e-14a58d774219> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "IndexedGraph twin for RDF list traversal" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/7c9de607-eccf-43da-802e-14a58d774219> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#resultsIn> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/3d7c8c35-ddcd-488e-97a4-cfec644fc194> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/7c9de607-eccf-43da-802e-14a58d774219> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#resultsIn> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/d0d876e5-a4d9-42a5-81bd-ec743e65f34b> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/7c9de607-eccf-43da-802e-14a58d774219> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#resultsIn> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/de45f566-1223-4fd2-9681-f969baab1c2f> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/8f7b36d6-b754-4f7e-b1f0-196c92945ea2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/8f7b36d6-b754-4f7e-b1f0-196c92945ea2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Term-valued leaves restore memory efficiency in TripleIndex" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/8f7b36d6-b754-4f7e-b1f0-196c92945ea2> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/8f7b36d6-b754-4f7e-b1f0-196c92945ea2> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "TripleIndex's SPO/PSO/OSP second-level leaves store only the \"remaining\" Term component again instead of the full Triple: TripleSet (Set Triple) / TripleMap (Map Term TripleSet) are renamed and retyped back to TermSet (Set Term) / TermSetMap (Map Term TermSet), reversing the \"Triple-valued leaves in TripleIndex\" decision. SPO/PSO leaves now store just the object Term; OSP leaves store just the predicate Term. indexed-graph-add's three index-update blocks now do `(set-put obj-set o)` for spo/pso and `(set-put pred-set p)` for osp instead of `(set-put triple-set t)`. Every read path that used to push the stored Triple reference directly now reconstructs it via `(record-new Triple (subject s) (predicate p) (object o))` at the point of match — see indexed-graph-match, indexed-graph-for-each, indexed-graph-contains (now `(set-has obj-set o)`), indexed-graph-subjects (now `(set-has pred-set pred)`), and indexed-graph-objects (now direct `(for-each (o obj-set) (list-push result o))`). Evidence: src/index.slop diff, commit 06821168e146300f6a7a440650ff8d0bf5aa7b44 (\"memory usage improvements for IndexedGraph\")." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/8f7b36d6-b754-4f7e-b1f0-196c92945ea2> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/8f7b36d6-b754-4f7e-b1f0-196c92945ea2> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasRationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/acfa5b30-93b2-4f92-920f-3517bdbaf2fd> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/8f7b36d6-b754-4f7e-b1f0-196c92945ea2> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-04-13T13:58:16Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/8f7b36d6-b754-4f7e-b1f0-196c92945ea2> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Term-valued leaves restore memory efficiency in TripleIndex" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/8f7b36d6-b754-4f7e-b1f0-196c92945ea2> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#isConstrainedBy> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/cc56ed06-7a6b-4ef4-8d5a-1feb56b986e5> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/8f7b36d6-b754-4f7e-b1f0-196c92945ea2> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#supersedes> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/5bdf80d4-cb1f-45ad-8e95-98f4356fee47> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/8f7b36d6-b754-4f7e-b1f0-196c92945ea2> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#weighs> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Alternative/bf8747c0-87fd-412b-a4a1-2134188018d5> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/98f6df58-7ca4-432e-8809-4e28875d5002> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/98f6df58-7ca4-432e-8809-4e28875d5002> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "N3 parser layered on top of the Turtle parser" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/98f6df58-7ca4-432e-8809-4e28875d5002> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/98f6df58-7ca4-432e-8809-4e28875d5002> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "N3ParseContext embeds a TtlParseContext rather than defining an independent character-stream/context of its own: `(type N3ParseContext (record (ttl-ctx TtlParseContext) (formula-counter FormulaId) (in-formula Bool) (current-formula-id (Option FormulaId))))`. n3.slop imports parse-iri-ref, parse-prefixed-name, parse-blank-node, parse-literal, parse-term, parse-directive, and parse-triple directly from the ttl module and reuses them for the Turtle-compatible parts of N3 syntax; only formulas (`{...}`), quick variables (`?x`), and path expressions (`!`/`^`) get N3-specific parsing code. Evidence: src/parse/n3.slop header comment \"N3 is a superset of Turtle with formulas, rules, and additional syntax\", the `(import ttl (PrefixMap TtlParseContext make-prefix-map ... parse-term parse-directive parse-triple ...))` line, and N3Term's `(n3-rdf Term)` variant which wraps the Turtle-level Term unchanged rather than redefining term kinds for N3." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/98f6df58-7ca4-432e-8809-4e28875d5002> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/98f6df58-7ca4-432e-8809-4e28875d5002> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-02-02T07:23:10Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/98f6df58-7ca4-432e-8809-4e28875d5002> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "N3 parser layered on top of the Turtle parser" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/a858856e-b791-40cc-a001-155678701d1e> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/a858856e-b791-40cc-a001-155678701d1e> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Lookahead-gated keyword dispatch for true/false/a in term parsing" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/a858856e-b791-40cc-a001-155678701d1e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/a858856e-b791-40cc-a001-155678701d1e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "parse-term's single-character cond dispatch in src/parse/ttl.slop no longer treats every token starting with 't' or 'f' as an unconditional boolean literal, and now also special-cases a bare 'a' token as the Turtle rdf:type keyword shortcut. For 't'/'f' it peeks 4-5 chars ahead to confirm an exact \"true\"/\"false\" spelling immediately followed by a non-name-continuation delimiter (not alnum, ':', '_', or '-') before calling parse-boolean-literal; otherwise it falls through to parse-prefixed-name. For 'a' it peeks one char ahead: if that char is whitespace (space/tab/LF/CR) it directly returns the rdf:type IRI (http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type) and advances state by one; otherwise it falls through to parse-prefixed-name. Rationale: the prior dispatch `((or (== c 116) (== c 102)) (parse-boolean-literal arena ctx))` matched on the first character alone, so any prefixed name starting with 't' or 'f' (e.g. \"tag:\", \"foaf:\") was mis-parsed as an attempted boolean literal; separately, no dispatch existed at all for a bare \"a\" token, so parsing \"a\" (the rdf:type shorthand) always fell through to parse-prefixed-name, which requires a following ':' and thus could never succeed for the shorthand. Evidence: commit 1e3d0618f7, src/parse/ttl.slop parse-term — replacement of the combined `(or (== c 116) (== c 102))` arm with separate 't'/'f' branches doing lookahead via state-peek-n, and the new `(== c 97)` branch constructing the rdf:type IRI directly." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/a858856e-b791-40cc-a001-155678701d1e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/a858856e-b791-40cc-a001-155678701d1e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-02-07T04:50:55Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/a858856e-b791-40cc-a001-155678701d1e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Lookahead-gated keyword dispatch for true/false/a in term parsing" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/a858856e-b791-40cc-a001-155678701d1e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#weighs> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Alternative/12cc6fa9-f2e0-40b0-afda-b6b28661dbc3> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/a858856e-b791-40cc-a001-155678701d1e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#weighs> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Alternative/5e727225-0deb-421a-a94f-02b9a18a8cb4> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/abcefc58-5160-4a33-a016-d4bfdfed41fe> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/abcefc58-5160-4a33-a016-d4bfdfed41fe> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Idempotent dedup guard in indexed-graph-add" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/abcefc58-5160-4a33-a016-d4bfdfed41fe> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/abcefc58-5160-4a33-a016-d4bfdfed41fe> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "indexed-graph-add now checks indexed-graph-contains(g, t) first and returns g unchanged if the triple is already present, instead of unconditionally inserting into the triples list and the three SPO/PSO/OSP index maps. Evidence: src/index.slop, indexed-graph-add's new lines \"(when (indexed-graph-contains g t) (return g))\" under the comment \";; Skip if already present (dedup)\", inserted before the existing (let ((s ...) (p ...) (o ...)) ...) index-update block." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/abcefc58-5160-4a33-a016-d4bfdfed41fe> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/abcefc58-5160-4a33-a016-d4bfdfed41fe> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-02-04T23:47:59Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/abcefc58-5160-4a33-a016-d4bfdfed41fe> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Idempotent dedup guard in indexed-graph-add" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/abcefc58-5160-4a33-a016-d4bfdfed41fe> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#resultsIn> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/069d1839-bdfc-4548-90d6-65c915a6c1c4> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/abcefc58-5160-4a33-a016-d4bfdfed41fe> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#weighs> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Alternative/2dafedf1-0164-439a-9d29-19f6aace998c> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/afb5a0a3-e99d-4806-b351-4e9d79d128ec> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/afb5a0a3-e99d-4806-b351-4e9d79d128ec> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Turtle PN_LOCAL allows embedded dots via lookahead" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/afb5a0a3-e99d-4806-b351-4e9d79d128ec> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/afb5a0a3-e99d-4806-b351-4e9d79d128ec> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "New parse-pn-local (src/parse/ttl.slop) parses a prefixed name's local part with dot-aware lookahead instead of a plain is-pn-chars scan: it parses a pn-chars segment, then if the next char is '.' it peeks one further char — if that's also a valid pn-char, it consumes the dot and continues parsing the next segment (allowing embedded/mid-name dots); if the dot would be the trailing character before a non-pn-char, it stops without consuming the dot. parse-prefixed-name's local-result binding switched from directly calling `(parse-while arena s2 is-pn-chars)` to calling `(parse-pn-local arena s2)`. Rationale: the prior plain scan terminated the local name at the first '.' unconditionally, rejecting valid Turtle prefixed names containing embedded dots — the W3C Turtle PN_LOCAL grammar production permits '.' anywhere in the local part except as the trailing character. Evidence: commit 1e3d0618f7, src/parse/ttl.slop, new `(fn parse-pn-local ...)` under `(@intent \"Parse local part of prefixed name, allowing dots that aren't the last char\")`." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/afb5a0a3-e99d-4806-b351-4e9d79d128ec> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/afb5a0a3-e99d-4806-b351-4e9d79d128ec> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-02-07T04:50:55Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/afb5a0a3-e99d-4806-b351-4e9d79d128ec> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Turtle PN_LOCAL allows embedded dots via lookahead" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/b1de6788-5d5c-4867-b441-6328ef918b45> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/b1de6788-5d5c-4867-b441-6328ef918b45> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Postcondition pruning in indexed-graph-add and term-eq" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/b1de6788-5d5c-4867-b441-6328ef918b45> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/b1de6788-5d5c-4867-b441-6328ef918b45> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Two runtime-checked `@post` contracts were deleted for performance in this commit: indexed-graph-add's `(@post (indexed-graph-contains $result t))` (asserting the just-added triple is present in the returned graph) and term-eq's `(@post (== $result (== a b)))`. Both sit on hot paths — indexed-graph-add runs once per parsed triple, and term-eq is now called even more often per operation than before (each TripleSet membership/hash check now runs triple-eq, which calls term-eq three times — once per subject/predicate/object — versus the single term-eq call a bare Term-set operation needed), so the per-call cost of re-verifying these postconditions at runtime is magnified by the same commit's TripleSet leaf-storage change. Evidence: src/index.slop — the removed `(@post (indexed-graph-contains $result t))` line in indexed-graph-add; src/rdf.slop — the removed `(@post (== $result (== a b)))` line in term-eq (the @example lines for term-eq are otherwise unchanged)." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/b1de6788-5d5c-4867-b441-6328ef918b45> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "superseded" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/b1de6788-5d5c-4867-b441-6328ef918b45> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-02-05T18:00:36Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/b1de6788-5d5c-4867-b441-6328ef918b45> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Postcondition pruning in indexed-graph-add and term-eq" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/b1de6788-5d5c-4867-b441-6328ef918b45> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#resultsIn> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/7ebca832-f69a-4d79-bbe3-223bbfba7967> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/bdb9868e-ee20-4208-be2f-13b034eebb8d> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/bdb9868e-ee20-4208-be2f-13b034eebb8d> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "serialize-triple-term builds its output with a string-concat chain" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/bdb9868e-ee20-4208-be2f-13b034eebb8d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/bdb9868e-ee20-4208-be2f-13b034eebb8d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "serialize-triple-term assembles `<<( s p o )>>` from a right-nested chain of six string-concat calls instead of one string-build over a seven-element list. Why: the contract verifier models string-concat (length of the result is the sum of the operands, and a non-empty operand gives a non-empty result) but has no model for string-build, so the function's `(@post (> (string-len $result) 0))` was unprovable and `slop verify` reported it failed. This was not an upgrade regression: the June-2026 verifier module failed the same contract, so the function had never verified since it was written. The rewrite matches how serialize-blank and serialize-quick-var already build their output. Evidence: src/serialize/serialize-ttl.slop serialize-triple-term; `slop verify` on 2026-09-12 reports it verified." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/bdb9868e-ee20-4208-be2f-13b034eebb8d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/bdb9868e-ee20-4208-be2f-13b034eebb8d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-09-12T04:25:04.906511Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/bdb9868e-ee20-4208-be2f-13b034eebb8d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "serialize-triple-term builds its output with a string-concat chain" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/bdb9868e-ee20-4208-be2f-13b034eebb8d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#resultsIn> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/7331534f-ff1e-4adc-b71a-a13047603c78> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/bdb9868e-ee20-4208-be2f-13b034eebb8d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#weighs> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Alternative/dbe6719f-075a-450b-99a6-538b21479c35> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/c09ecf18-b7cd-42f9-b4ba-419e498f61ed> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/c09ecf18-b7cd-42f9-b4ba-419e498f61ed> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Callback-based streaming hook for TTL parsing" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/c09ecf18-b7cd-42f9-b4ba-419e498f61ed> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/c09ecf18-b7cd-42f9-b4ba-419e498f61ed> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "parse-ttl-string-for-each-triple and parse-ttl-file-for-each-triple are new public parse entry points that take a `(callback (Fn (Triple) Unit))` and invoke it once per triple as it is parsed, via new parse-object-list-for-each-triple / parse-predicate-object-list-for-each-triple / emit-triples helpers, returning only a triple count instead of requiring callers to first parse into a full Graph via parse-ttl-string/parse-ttl-file and then iterate over it themselves. This gives custom/downstream parsers a way to consume triples as they stream out of the Turtle grammar rather than after the whole document has been materialized into a Graph.\n\nEvidence: commit 6c55d4a (PR #6 \"parser-hook\", body \"add parse hook for custom parsers\"); src/parse/ttl.slop's new `StreamTriplesResult` record, and the new `emit-triples`, `parse-object-list-for-each-triple`, `parse-predicate-object-list-for-each-triple`, `parse-ttl-string-for-each-triple`, `parse-ttl-file-for-each-triple` functions, all added alongside (not replacing) the existing parse-ttl-string/parse-ttl-file Graph-building path." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/c09ecf18-b7cd-42f9-b4ba-419e498f61ed> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/c09ecf18-b7cd-42f9-b4ba-419e498f61ed> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-06-29T18:31:52Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/c09ecf18-b7cd-42f9-b4ba-419e498f61ed> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Callback-based streaming hook for TTL parsing" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/c09ecf18-b7cd-42f9-b4ba-419e498f61ed> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#resultsIn> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/e1175d96-8d8e-49a2-b942-7d6ac97b6ac3> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/c09ecf18-b7cd-42f9-b4ba-419e498f61ed> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#weighs> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Alternative/aaed7741-694d-4dc6-805d-399735f22e85> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/c6fa135a-e1af-4a51-8da6-e3193d998467> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/c6fa135a-e1af-4a51-8da6-e3193d998467> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "RDF 1.2 annotation blocks reify via rdf:reifies" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/c6fa135a-e1af-4a51-8da6-e3193d998467> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/c6fa135a-e1af-4a51-8da6-e3193d998467> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Turtle `{| pred obj ; pred obj |}` annotation blocks immediately following a triple's object are parsed by minting a fresh blank-node reifier, emitting `(reifier rdf:reifies <<( base-subject base-predicate base-object )>>)`, then parsing the block's own predicate-object list against that reifier as subject — rather than leaving `{| |}` unparsed or using classic RDF 1.0 reification vocabulary (rdf:type rdf:Statement / rdf:subject / rdf:predicate / rdf:object). A triple's object can be followed by zero or more such blocks in a loop, each producing its own independent reifier. Directly motivated by real-world ingestion: the new examples/software_eng.ttl fixture (output of an external \"Trivyn Ontology Pipeline\") attaches per-axiom `trivyn:confidence`/`skos:historyNote`/`dcterms:created` provenance metadata to `rdfs:subClassOf` axioms using exactly this `{| ... |}` syntax, which this parser could not previously ingest at all. Depends on this same commit's Term union extension (new term-triple variant) since the reifies-object is built via make-triple-term. Evidence: commit b48ba5c, src/parse/ttl.slop's new `parse-annotation` function and its call site inside `parse-object-list`'s new \"zero or more {| ... |} blocks\" while-loop; test/test-ttl-parser.slop's new \"RDF 1.2 Annotation {| |}\" test asserting graph-size 4 and exactly one `rdf:reifies` triple for a single annotated triple, plus a second test confirming annotation blocks compose with semicolon-separated predicate lists." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/c6fa135a-e1af-4a51-8da6-e3193d998467> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/c6fa135a-e1af-4a51-8da6-e3193d998467> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-06-25T20:02:50Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/c6fa135a-e1af-4a51-8da6-e3193d998467> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "RDF 1.2 annotation blocks reify via rdf:reifies" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/c6fa135a-e1af-4a51-8da6-e3193d998467> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#resultsIn> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/82e03c9a-b86f-4ac9-8af7-8b11560afb8c> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/d6c0f11d-74b4-462d-9283-c7560bc30875> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/d6c0f11d-74b4-462d-9283-c7560bc30875> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "SPO/PSO/OSP dispatch restored in indexed-graph-match" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/d6c0f11d-74b4-462d-9283-c7560bc30875> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/d6c0f11d-74b4-462d-9283-c7560bc30875> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "indexed-graph-match again dispatches through the graph's SPO/PSO/OSP indexes based on which of subject/predicate/object are bound, replacing the unconditional linear scan over g.triples introduced by \"Linear-scan filtering replaces index dispatch in indexed-graph-match\". The new nested `(match subj ((some s) (match (map-get (. (. g index) spo) s) ...)) ((none) (match pred ((some p) (match (map-get (. (. g index) pso) p) ...)) ((none) (match obj ((some o) (match (map-get (. (. g index) osp) o) ...)) ((none) (for-each (t (. g triples)) ...)))))))` dispatch mirrors the structure indexed-graph-for-each already uses, and walks only the relevant SPO/PSO/OSP leaf(s); only the fully-unbound case still falls back to scanning g.triples. Evidence: src/index.slop — the single `(for-each (t (. g triples)) ...)` block with per-field term-eq filtering, under comments \"Simple filtering approach - iterate existing triples, no allocation of new Triple objects\" / \"Trade O(1) index lookup for zero memory allocation per query\", is deleted and replaced under the new comment \"Use index-based dispatch for O(1) lookup instead of full scan\". Commit 35d7d249, \"performance improvements\"." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/d6c0f11d-74b4-462d-9283-c7560bc30875> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/d6c0f11d-74b4-462d-9283-c7560bc30875> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasRationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/53994bb8-7fab-4d6f-8163-e825cc46f579> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/d6c0f11d-74b4-462d-9283-c7560bc30875> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-02-06T18:30:48Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/d6c0f11d-74b4-462d-9283-c7560bc30875> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "SPO/PSO/OSP dispatch restored in indexed-graph-match" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/d6c0f11d-74b4-462d-9283-c7560bc30875> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#isConstrainedBy> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/cc56ed06-7a6b-4ef4-8d5a-1feb56b986e5> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
