<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/d79c1545-815e-4eca-a351-6f098aa17a02> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/d79c1545-815e-4eca-a351-6f098aa17a02> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Graph-threaded accumulation for TTL predicate-object lists" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/d79c1545-815e-4eca-a351-6f098aa17a02> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/d79c1545-815e-4eca-a351-6f098aa17a02> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Claim: a new GraphTriplesResult type plus parse-object-list-into-graph and parse-predicate-object-list-into-graph (src/parse/ttl.slop) thread the accumulating Graph itself through predicate-object-list parsing, appending each parsed triple straight into it via graph-add-unchecked as it's produced; the top-level per-statement call site in the main parse loop now calls parse-predicate-object-list-into-graph directly and takes `(. polr graph)` as the new graph, instead of calling the List-Triple-returning parse-predicate-object-list and merging its full `(. polr triples)` list into the graph afterward via graph-add-all.\n\nWhy: avoids building one `(List Triple)` per statement's predicate-object-list before a separate merge pass. Evidence: src/parse/ttl.slop diff — new `(type GraphTriplesResult (record (graph Graph) (ctx TtlParseContext)))`; new parse-object-list-into-graph/parse-predicate-object-list-into-graph fns; the top-level statement-parsing call site changing from `(let ((polr (? (parse-predicate-object-list arena (. sr ctx) (. sr term)))) ...) (do (set! g (graph-add-all arena g (. polr triples))) ...))` to `(let ((polr (? (parse-predicate-object-list-into-graph arena (. sr ctx) g (. sr term)))) ...) (do (set! g (. polr graph)) ...))`." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/d79c1545-815e-4eca-a351-6f098aa17a02> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/d79c1545-815e-4eca-a351-6f098aa17a02> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-06-29T00:06:21Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/d79c1545-815e-4eca-a351-6f098aa17a02> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Graph-threaded accumulation for TTL predicate-object lists" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/d79c1545-815e-4eca-a351-6f098aa17a02> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#resultsIn> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/cdbb0ab2-9a38-41b7-bf49-c55257b41596> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/d79c1545-815e-4eca-a351-6f098aa17a02> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#weighs> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Alternative/1432d78d-d7d0-4077-940c-2e1bd3492d0e> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/da12bd2a-a787-4dc1-98aa-bd3a81266f30> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/da12bd2a-a787-4dc1-98aa-bd3a81266f30> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Term constructors are @pure" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/da12bd2a-a787-4dc1-98aa-bd3a81266f30> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/da12bd2a-a787-4dc1-98aa-bd3a81266f30> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "make-iri, make-blank, make-literal and make-triple in src/rdf.slop carry (@pure) beside (@alloc arena): each is a single union-new or record-new of its `in` arguments with no side effects. make-triple-term stays unmarked because it arena-allocates a Triple and writes through the pointer.\n\nWhy: SLOP's verifier proves @loop-invariants (slop#228) but will not check an invariant that calls a non-@pure function inside a quantifier, nor one that reads a Term (collection state, via the (term-triple (Ptr Triple)) variant) while the loop body calls a non-@pure function. growl's rule loops build triples with make-triple and name predicates with make-iri, so their invariants reported \"could not check loop invariant ... (it calls make-iri, which is not @pure ...)\"; with the annotations growl's dt-type1, dt-type2, prp-ap, cls-thing and cls-nothing1 invariants are proved and a broken body is caught.\n\nConstraint honoured: slop-sys vendors slop-rdf's generated C, so the change had to leave it byte-identical. Evidence (2026-09-30, commit a5de195 on branch pure-term-constructors): slop-compiler transpile with the v0.3.0 release compiler gives identical output for rdf.slop alone (25,991 bytes) and for all twelve vendored modules together (444,576 bytes), and rdf.slop is also identical under current slop main; slop test (116), all test/*.slop suites and slop verify (78 verified, the pre-existing common.slop failure, 1 unknown) are unchanged." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/da12bd2a-a787-4dc1-98aa-bd3a81266f30> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/da12bd2a-a787-4dc1-98aa-bd3a81266f30> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-09-30T06:37:54.340336Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/da12bd2a-a787-4dc1-98aa-bd3a81266f30> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Term constructors are @pure" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/da12bd2a-a787-4dc1-98aa-bd3a81266f30> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#isMotivatedBy> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/f9a5a045-5834-4b91-84f6-77b00174148a> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/da12bd2a-a787-4dc1-98aa-bd3a81266f30> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#resultsIn> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/323a0342-40a0-4c6a-8874-cbb015d88eb3> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/da12bd2a-a787-4dc1-98aa-bd3a81266f30> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#resultsIn> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/5d2b96d3-5880-403c-9acb-4c61fecc48fb> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/dc194798-e290-471f-8e76-65fc0dbcc83e> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/dc194798-e290-471f-8e76-65fc0dbcc83e> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "POS index added to TripleIndex" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/dc194798-e290-471f-8e76-65fc0dbcc83e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/dc194798-e290-471f-8e76-65fc0dbcc83e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "TripleIndex gains a fourth index, POS (Map Term TermSetMap) mapping predicate -> object -> Set[subject], alongside the existing SPO/PSO/OSP, giving direct O(1) subject-set lookup for queries with predicate and object bound but subject free. Previously such queries (in indexed-graph-match, indexed-graph-for-each, and indexed-graph-subjects) walked the PSO or OSP index's full subject-map for the bound field and did a set-has check per subject, so cost scaled with the number of subjects of the predicate (e.g. every rdf:type assertion) rather than with the actual match count.\n\nEvidence: commit ec4e364a1e, src/index.slop — new `(pos (Map Term TermSetMap))` field on TripleIndex plus its `(pos (map-new arena Term TermSetMap))` initializer; indexed-graph-add gains a POS index-maintenance block mirroring the SPO/PSO/OSP ones; indexed-graph-match's and indexed-graph-for-each's P+O-bound arm changes from PSO's `(for-each ((s term-set) subj-map) (when (set-has term-set o) ...))` to `(map-get pos-idx p)` -> `(map-get obj-map o)` -> direct `(for-each (s subj-set) ...)`; indexed-graph-subjects changes from OSP's `(for-each ((s pred-set) subj-map) (when (set-has pred-set pred) (list-push result s)))` to the same direct POS lookup. New doc comment: \"POS gives subjects directly for (?, p, o) queries, avoiding a scan of all subjects of p (e.g. every rdf:type assertion) in the predicate+object case.\" Commit message: \"Fix to the indexer\" (PR #5)." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/dc194798-e290-471f-8e76-65fc0dbcc83e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/dc194798-e290-471f-8e76-65fc0dbcc83e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-06-29T17:07:28Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
