<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/05075f15-da22-4f30-96f3-f33b9ee2dd0c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-02-07T03:15:11Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/05075f15-da22-4f30-96f3-f33b9ee2dd0c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "serialize-ttl-stream duplicates serialize-ttl-string's subject/predicate/object grouping logic (the same same-subject/same-predicate/different-subject punctuation-choice branching) as a second, separately-maintained implementation driving direct fwrite calls instead of string-concat, and bypasses the file module's file-write-line abstraction by talking to a raw FILE* handle via FFI." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/069d1839-bdfc-4548-90d6-65c915a6c1c4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Consequence> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/069d1839-bdfc-4548-90d6-65c915a6c1c4> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Since indexed-graph-match (per this same commit's linear-scan change) now returns triples by scanning g.triples directly rather than via deduped index Sets, this dedup guard is what prevents indexed-graph-match from returning the same triple twice when indexed-graph-add is called more than once with an identical triple." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
