<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/081378ce-dbc5-405b-acee-ba03d72b1235> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "The non-streaming parse-ttl-string / parse-ttl-file produce the same Graph with fewer allocations (views as lookup keys, one allocation per prefixed name and per escaped literal)." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/0a1a482f-6838-4f0e-b9d7-ec7074407da5> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Consequence> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/0a1a482f-6838-4f0e-b9d7-ec7074407da5> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Callers of indexed-graph-for-each can now rely on a trusted, contract-verifier-recognized guarantee that every triple reaching their callback satisfies the query's subject/predicate/object filters and is a real member of the graph, without needing to re-derive this from the SPO/PSO/OSP index-dispatch implementation themselves." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/0a1a482f-6838-4f0e-b9d7-ec7074407da5> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
