<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/a1d22b58-6544-4735-9bb3-c1d6f55cdb1c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-02-06T21:28:34Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/a1d22b58-6544-4735-9bb3-c1d6f55cdb1c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Each level of the SPO/PSO/OSP index update in indexed-graph-add now performs a single map-get dispatched via match instead of a map-has probe plus a conditional map-put plus an unconditional map-get, reducing map operations per index level on every triple insert." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/a57c5f15-39b7-4b97-8096-249703fe6755> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Consequence> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/a57c5f15-39b7-4b97-8096-249703fe6755> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Using is-pn-chars for language tags is more permissive than BCP47 syntax actually allows: it also accepts an underscore ('_', 95) within the tag body, even though BCP47 subtags are hyphen-separated only, so a malformed tag like \"en_US\" would now lex without error instead of being rejected." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/a57c5f15-39b7-4b97-8096-249703fe6755> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/a57c5f15-39b7-4b97-8096-249703fe6755> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/a57c5f15-39b7-4b97-8096-249703fe6755> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-02-13T03:03:21Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/a57c5f15-39b7-4b97-8096-249703fe6755> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Using is-pn-chars for language tags is more permissive than BCP47 syntax actually allows: it also accepts an underscore ('_', 95) within the tag body, even though BCP47 subtags are hyphen-separated only, so a malformed tag like \"en_US\" would now lex without error instead of being rejected." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/b12354f4-127d-41bb-ab96-05888d2d11ff> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Consequence> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/b12354f4-127d-41bb-ab96-05888d2d11ff> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "The per-field matching filter logic (subject/predicate/object equality checks via term-eq) is now duplicated verbatim between indexed-graph-match and indexed-graph-for-each rather than factored into a shared helper, since both were introduced/changed in this same commit as separate for-each loops over g.triples." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/b12354f4-127d-41bb-ab96-05888d2d11ff> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
