<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/f40405f6-c310-4afd-a6f7-32547e566690> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "TtlParseContext's new `blank-labels` field had to be threaded through essentially every `record-new TtlParseContext` call site across ttl.slop and n3.slop (~20 call sites touched in this commit), extending the per-field record-new duplication already noted as a consequence of the 'Immutable ParseState threading' pattern (no record-update/spread syntax in Slop)." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/f8712f81-d7b1-471d-a01e-68d2ff922604> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Consequence> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/f8712f81-d7b1-471d-a01e-68d2ff922604> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "indexed-graph-match becomes O(n) regardless of binding" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/f8712f81-d7b1-471d-a01e-68d2ff922604> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/f8712f81-d7b1-471d-a01e-68d2ff922604> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Every indexed-graph-match call is now O(n) in the number of triples in g, even when subject/predicate/object are fully bound, since the SPO/PSO/OSP indexes built by indexed-graph-add are no longer consulted for matching — only (unchanged) for contains/subjects/objects. This forfeits the O(1)-average lookup benefit from the original indexing decision in exchange for avoiding per-query Triple allocation. Evidence: src/index.slop indexed-graph-match's replacement for-each loop scans g.triples unconditionally; inline comment \"Trade O(1) index lookup for zero memory allocation per query\"." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/f8712f81-d7b1-471d-a01e-68d2ff922604> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "superseded" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/f8712f81-d7b1-471d-a01e-68d2ff922604> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-02-04T23:47:59Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/f8712f81-d7b1-471d-a01e-68d2ff922604> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "indexed-graph-match becomes O(n) regardless of binding" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/f8712f81-d7b1-471d-a01e-68d2ff922604> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#resultsFrom> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/1afcbec8-fd6c-4396-838a-321b5c6e58fa> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/04276f2e-77cc-4f16-a1f1-5851383e92ef> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Constraint> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/04276f2e-77cc-4f16-a1f1-5851383e92ef> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Streaming TTL callback Triple is valid only during the call" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/04276f2e-77cc-4f16-a1f1-5851383e92ef> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#constrains> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/4259ec3f-7488-4b1c-a390-0e25f7ad6c60> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/04276f2e-77cc-4f16-a1f1-5851383e92ef> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#constrains> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/c09ecf18-b7cd-42f9-b4ba-419e498f61ed> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/04276f2e-77cc-4f16-a1f1-5851383e92ef> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/04276f2e-77cc-4f16-a1f1-5851383e92ef> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "A Triple passed to the callback of parse-ttl-string-for-each-triple or parse-ttl-file-for-each-triple — its IRI and literal strings, and the Triple behind a triple term — is valid only during that callback. Each statement is parsed in a scratch arena that is reset after its triples are delivered, so a callback that keeps a term must copy its strings. Blank node ids are plain ints and may be kept. Delivery order is document order (a term's nested triples, then the triple using it, then its annotations) and blank nodes are numbered from 0 per parse, anonymous nodes and collection cells sharing one counter.\n\nEvidence: the contract comment above parse-ttl-string-for-each-triple in src/parse/ttl.slop; test/test-ttl-stream.slop (\"Callback contract: copies outlive the parse\", \"Blank node numbering\"). HOWL's encoded-add (howl/src/termstore.slop) copies every string it keeps via own-plain-term/copy-string, so it satisfies this." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/04276f2e-77cc-4f16-a1f1-5851383e92ef> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/04276f2e-77cc-4f16-a1f1-5851383e92ef> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-09-30T04:14:05.282239Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/04276f2e-77cc-4f16-a1f1-5851383e92ef> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Streaming TTL callback Triple is valid only during the call" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/0c3057dd-1f70-410b-b6ee-a7681e79671c> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Constraint> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/0c3057dd-1f70-410b-b6ee-a7681e79671c> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Parser character model restricted to ASCII (0-127)" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/0c3057dd-1f70-410b-b6ee-a7681e79671c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#constrains> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/98f6df58-7ca4-432e-8809-4e28875d5002> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/0c3057dd-1f70-410b-b6ee-a7681e79671c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#constrains> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/e1779018-34aa-4c27-aada-eca6b934e5ad> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/0c3057dd-1f70-410b-b6ee-a7681e79671c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/0c3057dd-1f70-410b-b6ee-a7681e79671c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "The shared parsing primitives operate on single \"characters\" typed (Int 0 .. 127) — src/parse/common.slop's `state-peek` and `state-peek-n` both declare `(@spec (... -> (Int 0 .. 127)))`, and src/parse/ttl.slop's EscapeResult record types its decoded `char` field the same way — so the Turtle/N3 parsers model input as a stream of ASCII code points rather than Unicode scalar values. Evidence: `(fn state-peek ((in state ParseState)) ... (@spec ((ParseState) -> (Int 0 .. 127))) ...)` and `state-peek-n`'s identical return-type annotation in src/parse/common.slop; `(type EscapeResult (record (char (Int 0 .. 127)) (ctx TtlParseContext)))` in src/parse/ttl.slop." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/0c3057dd-1f70-410b-b6ee-a7681e79671c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/0c3057dd-1f70-410b-b6ee-a7681e79671c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-02-02T07:23:10Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/0c3057dd-1f70-410b-b6ee-a7681e79671c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Parser character model restricted to ASCII (0-127)" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/118de051-16f0-4350-8f1a-09a958691d46> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Constraint> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/118de051-16f0-4350-8f1a-09a958691d46> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Slop arena defaults to a 256MB global cap" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/118de051-16f0-4350-8f1a-09a958691d46> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#constrains> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/0fea10c1-0a41-4526-978e-bf83479a4e27> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/118de051-16f0-4350-8f1a-09a958691d46> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/118de051-16f0-4350-8f1a-09a958691d46> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Slop's arena allocator enforces a default global cap of 256MB; growing an arena past that size for large workloads requires building with --no-arena-cap. Evidence: bench/parse-meteorites.slop's new inline comment above its `(with-arena 67108864 ...)` call: \"Start with 64MB; benchmark builds should use --no-arena-cap so the arena can grow for large graphs without hitting the default 256MB global cap.\"" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/118de051-16f0-4350-8f1a-09a958691d46> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/118de051-16f0-4350-8f1a-09a958691d46> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-06-29T14:07:04Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/118de051-16f0-4350-8f1a-09a958691d46> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Slop arena defaults to a 256MB global cap" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/ae9db45d-d658-4721-9a5f-2cba7e892d1e> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Constraint> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/ae9db45d-d658-4721-9a5f-2cba7e892d1e> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Graph.size mirrors triples list length" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/ae9db45d-d658-4721-9a5f-2cba7e892d1e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/ae9db45d-d658-4721-9a5f-2cba7e892d1e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Graph carries a cached `size` field that must always equal `list-len(triples)` — enforced by an explicit `@invariant` on the `Graph` record type. Evidence: src/rdf.slop, `(type Graph (record (triples (List Triple)) (size GraphSize)) (@invariant (== size (list-len triples))))`; graph-add/graph-remove/graph-size all keep the two in sync (graph-size's own @post reasserts `(== $result (list-len g.triples))`)." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/ae9db45d-d658-4721-9a5f-2cba7e892d1e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/ae9db45d-d658-4721-9a5f-2cba7e892d1e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-01-20T17:26:41Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/ae9db45d-d658-4721-9a5f-2cba7e892d1e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Graph.size mirrors triples list length" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/cc56ed06-7a6b-4ef4-8d5a-1feb56b986e5> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Constraint> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/cc56ed06-7a6b-4ef4-8d5a-1feb56b986e5> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "IndexedGraph query correctness axioms" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/cc56ed06-7a6b-4ef4-8d5a-1feb56b986e5> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#constrains> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/5d67c78c-0166-4c2b-b412-12a8d839fee0> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/cc56ed06-7a6b-4ef4-8d5a-1feb56b986e5> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#constrains> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/787f1ae4-9ca5-4758-8157-8f3763d5d7e0> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/cc56ed06-7a6b-4ef4-8d5a-1feb56b986e5> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#constrains> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/abcefc58-5160-4a33-a016-d4bfdfed41fe> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/cc56ed06-7a6b-4ef4-8d5a-1feb56b986e5> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#constrains> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/b1de6788-5d5c-4867-b441-6328ef918b45> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/cc56ed06-7a6b-4ef4-8d5a-1feb56b986e5> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/cc56ed06-7a6b-4ef4-8d5a-1feb56b986e5> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "indexed-graph-contains and indexed-graph-match must agree with a linear scan over g.triples: contains(g,t) holds iff some t2 in g.triples has triple-eq(t,t2); match's result list is a subset of g.triples, every returned triple satisfies indexed-graph-contains (bridging match to contains), every returned triple matches any bound subj/pred/obj argument on that field, and when subj/pred/obj are all none the result must contain every triple in g.triples. These are declared with `@assume` rather than `@post` — trusted axioms bridging the SPO/PSO/OSP index representation back to the ground-truth triples list, not properties proven from the index's map/set structure. Evidence: src/index.slop — indexed-graph-contains's two new `@assume (implies ...)` lines under the comment \"Semantic axioms: contains iff triple exists in g.triples\"; indexed-graph-match's five new `@assume` lines under comments \"Results are subset of all triples in graph\", \"Results are contained in graph (bridges match → contains)\", the three per-field filtering axioms, and the all-none membership axiom." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/cc56ed06-7a6b-4ef4-8d5a-1feb56b986e5> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/cc56ed06-7a6b-4ef4-8d5a-1feb56b986e5> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-01-29T04:39:04Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/cc56ed06-7a6b-4ef4-8d5a-1feb56b986e5> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "IndexedGraph query correctness axioms" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/0932b77e-504b-42c4-8e7c-52a0ebd57fe1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Lesson> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/0932b77e-504b-42c4-8e7c-52a0ebd57fe1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Untyped `(mut n 0)` captured by a closure is a C int behind an int64_t*" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/0932b77e-504b-42c4-8e7c-52a0ebd57fe1> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/0932b77e-504b-42c4-8e7c-52a0ebd57fe1> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "A SLOP local bound as `(mut n 0)` with no type is emitted as `__auto_type n = 0;` — a 32-bit C int — but a closure that captures it stores `int64_t* n = &(n)` in its env, so every read or write through the closure touches 8 bytes over a 4-byte slot. Symptom seen in test/test-ttl-stream.slop: `(list-get triples idx)` inside a streaming callback returned none for every index (the index read included garbage from the neighbouring `bad` counter), while the build and type check were clean. Workaround until slop fixes it: give closure-captured counters an explicit type, `(mut n Int 0)`. A local initialised from an Int-returning call (e.g. bench's `h` updated via hash-triple) came out int64_t and was fine. This is a slop transpiler bug (report upstream; don't work around it in library code)." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/0932b77e-504b-42c4-8e7c-52a0ebd57fe1> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/0932b77e-504b-42c4-8e7c-52a0ebd57fe1> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-09-30T04:14:19.648477Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/0932b77e-504b-42c4-8e7c-52a0ebd57fe1> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Untyped `(mut n 0)` captured by a closure is a C int behind an int64_t*" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/0932b77e-504b-42c4-8e7c-52a0ebd57fe1> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#learnedFrom> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/4259ec3f-7488-4b1c-a390-0e25f7ad6c60> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/26906c15-c90e-41d7-8b96-1ae5bec74507> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Lesson> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/26906c15-c90e-41d7-8b96-1ae5bec74507> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "list-push/map-put grow into the variable named `arena`" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/26906c15-c90e-41d7-8b96-1ae5bec74507> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/26906c15-c90e-41d7-8b96-1ae5bec74507> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "SLOP's list-push and map-put (and closure environments) allocate growth in the arena bound to a variable literally named `arena` in scope — not in the arena the list or map was created in. So when a statement is parsed with a scratch arena passed as `arena`, any push onto a long-lived structure (prefix bindings, the blank-label map) would grow into scratch and dangle after the reset. Grow long-lived structures only inside a helper whose `arena` parameter is the long-lived arena, called with that arena: ttl.slop's blank-labels-add is called with (. tbl arena); prefix-map-add is only called at the top level with the parse's long-lived arena.\n\nRelated: `?` and with-arena early exits do not free open arenas, so a scratch arena needs explicit arena-new/arena-free with match-based error paths. Evidence: resolve-arena-c-name / get-arena-for-list-push-expr in ~/code/slop/lib/compiler/transpiler/expr.slop; spec/LANGUAGE.md around lines 935-940." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/26906c15-c90e-41d7-8b96-1ae5bec74507> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/26906c15-c90e-41d7-8b96-1ae5bec74507> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-09-30T04:14:19.562384Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/26906c15-c90e-41d7-8b96-1ae5bec74507> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "list-push/map-put grow into the variable named `arena`" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/26906c15-c90e-41d7-8b96-1ae5bec74507> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#learnedFrom> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/4259ec3f-7488-4b1c-a390-0e25f7ad6c60> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/26906c15-c90e-41d7-8b96-1ae5bec74507> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#learnedFrom> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/52e7f143-3c47-4dfd-b7cb-4fce4e305c31> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/491e28d0-af0a-4dfa-bc86-1b963de61f80> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Lesson> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/491e28d0-af0a-4dfa-bc86-1b963de61f80> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Verifier drops a returned call's postcondition when an argument was assigned" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/491e28d0-af0a-4dfa-bc86-1b963de61f80> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/491e28d0-af0a-4dfa-bc86-1b963de61f80> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "The slop verifier (0.2.3, src/slop/verifier/contract_verifier.py `_process_direct_call_return` via `_collect_call_postconditions`) instantiates a callee's @post for a function whose body returns a direct call, but only when every argument is a parameter or a never-assigned let binding. If an argument is a `mut` local that any `set!` touched before the call, even one straight-line assignment, `binding_in_scope` marks the name versioned (per the #116/#118 guards) and the substituted postcondition is silently not asserted, so nothing about $result follows from the callee. Minimal repro: three functions returning `(state-with-position state offset ...)` with @post `{$result.offset >= state.offset}`; the one whose `offset` is an unassigned let verifies, the ones with `(set! offset (+ offset 1))` straight-line or in a while loop both fail with `fn_state-with-position_4=[else -> N]` in the counterexample. This is why skip-whitespace in src/parse/common.slop cannot verify its postcondition `(or (state-at-end $result) (not (is-space (state-peek $result))))` even after state-with-position gained field-mapping @posts, state-peek gained a char-at @post, and the while loop gained `(@loop-invariant (or (not done) (not (is-space (char-at input offset)))))`. A second, smaller gap: a call to a non-inlinable user function such as state-peek inside the contract being checked is translated as an uninterpreted function and its own @post is not instantiated there, so the caller's post must be phrased via char-at on the result fields to be provable even once the first gap is fixed. Both are slop verifier issues to fix upstream, not to work around in slop-rdf; the added helper contracts and loop invariant are true, pass at runtime, and stay in place for when the verifier can use them." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/491e28d0-af0a-4dfa-bc86-1b963de61f80> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/491e28d0-af0a-4dfa-bc86-1b963de61f80> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-09-12T04:25:13.582487Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/491e28d0-af0a-4dfa-bc86-1b963de61f80> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Verifier drops a returned call's postcondition when an argument was assigned" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/509a6a33-ecec-448e-b4b6-773c2be46b54> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Lesson> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/509a6a33-ecec-448e-b4b6-773c2be46b54> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "RDF list traversal truncates silently on malformed rest" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/509a6a33-ecec-448e-b4b6-773c2be46b54> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/509a6a33-ecec-448e-b4b6-773c2be46b54> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "`rdf-list-elements` stops collecting and returns whatever it has gathered so far when a list node has no `rdf:rest` triple, instead of raising an error — so a malformed/truncated RDF collection is indistinguishable from a well-formed short one via its return value alone. Evidence: src/list.slop, `rdf-list-elements`'s `while` loop: when the `rdf:rest` `graph-match` call returns zero triples, the code runs `(set! current nil-term)` with the inline comment `;; No rest, terminate` rather than signaling an error; likewise a missing `rdf:first` triple for the current node is silently skipped (`(when (> (list-len (. first-matches triples)) 0) ...)`) without surfacing that the head lacked the predicate. `rdf-list-contains` and `rdf-list-length` both build on `rdf-list-elements`, so they inherit the same silent-truncation behavior." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/509a6a33-ecec-448e-b4b6-773c2be46b54> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/509a6a33-ecec-448e-b4b6-773c2be46b54> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-01-23T07:28:17Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/509a6a33-ecec-448e-b4b6-773c2be46b54> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "RDF list traversal truncates silently on malformed rest" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/6ae8639d-31f1-4b30-a7c4-ee13a186f1f7> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Lesson> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/6ae8639d-31f1-4b30-a7c4-ee13a186f1f7> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "blank-labels field projection drops pushes without explicit rethread" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/6ae8639d-31f1-4b30-a7c4-ee13a186f1f7> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/6ae8639d-31f1-4b30-a7c4-ee13a186f1f7> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Corrects the prior Lesson: struct-field projection `(. ctx blank-labels)` must NOT be treated as a safely shared mutable reference for `list-push` — pushing onto it and discarding the projected value can lose the new binding. The fix binds the list to a `(mut labels (. ctx blank-labels))` local, pushes onto `labels`, and explicitly places `labels` into the new `TtlParseContext` record's `blank-labels` field, rather than trusting `(ctx-with-state (. gen ctx) ...)` to carry the mutation forward.\n\nWhy: the old `_:label` new-binding branch of `parse-blank-node` did `(list-push (. ctx blank-labels) (record-new BlankLabelBinding ...))` then `(ok (record-new TermTriplesResult ... (ctx (ctx-with-state (. gen ctx) (. label-result state)))))` — trusting the push to already be reflected in the forwarded context. The new inline comment in this commit states plainly: \"list-push on the struct field (. ctx blank-labels) mutates a by-value copy and would drop the binding, so bind the list to a mutable local and store it back.\"\n\nEvidence: commit 937461fe5b, src/parse/ttl.slop's rewritten `_:label` `(none)` arm: `(let ((gen (context-gen-blank-id arena ctx)) (mut labels (. ctx blank-labels))) (list-push labels (record-new BlankLabelBinding ...)) (ok (record-new TermTriplesResult ... (ctx (record-new TtlParseContext ... (blank-labels labels) ...)))))`; test/test-ttl-parser.slop's new \"Labeled Blank Node Coreference\" test parsing `_:x <p> <o1> .` then `_:x <p> <o2> .` and asserting `(graph-match arena g (some (make-blank arena 0)) (none) (none))` matches both triples." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/6ae8639d-31f1-4b30-a7c4-ee13a186f1f7> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/6ae8639d-31f1-4b30-a7c4-ee13a186f1f7> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasRationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/ce4889b0-97fe-470f-a24e-ed4979a7f46e> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/6ae8639d-31f1-4b30-a7c4-ee13a186f1f7> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-06-26T02:06:40Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/6ae8639d-31f1-4b30-a7c4-ee13a186f1f7> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "blank-labels field projection drops pushes without explicit rethread" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/6ae8639d-31f1-4b30-a7c4-ee13a186f1f7> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#learnedFrom> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/58d69b61-cacd-42a4-bf3c-5b616d359864> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/6ae8639d-31f1-4b30-a7c4-ee13a186f1f7> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#supersedes> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/8ef105c2-45fa-4729-912b-29a9ab655270> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/8bc2e113-cbf8-4eb9-babe-50140c7c07ee> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Lesson> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/8bc2e113-cbf8-4eb9-babe-50140c7c07ee> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "TTL escape parsing rejects \\u/\\U Unicode escapes" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/8bc2e113-cbf8-4eb9-babe-50140c7c07ee> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/8bc2e113-cbf8-4eb9-babe-50140c7c07ee> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "parse-escape-sequence in src/parse/ttl.slop only recognizes the six short ECHAR escapes — \\n(110), \\t(116), \\r(114), \\\\(92), \\\"(34), \\'(39) — and falls through to an 'invalid-escape ParseError for any other character following a backslash, including the \\uXXXX / \\UXXXXXXXX Unicode escapes required by the W3C Turtle STRING_LITERAL grammar. EscapeResult.char is typed (Int 0 .. 127), so even extending the cond arms could not currently return a decoded codepoint above 127 without widening that type first. Evidence: src/parse/ttl.slop, parse-escape-sequence's `cond` (six single-character branches then `(else (error (make-parse-error arena 'invalid-escape \"Invalid escape sequence\" ...)))`) and `(type EscapeResult (record (char (Int 0 .. 127)) (ctx TtlParseContext)))`." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/8bc2e113-cbf8-4eb9-babe-50140c7c07ee> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/8bc2e113-cbf8-4eb9-babe-50140c7c07ee> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-02-02T07:23:10Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/8bc2e113-cbf8-4eb9-babe-50140c7c07ee> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "TTL escape parsing rejects \\u/\\U Unicode escapes" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/8ef105c2-45fa-4729-912b-29a9ab655270> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Lesson> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/8ef105c2-45fa-4729-912b-29a9ab655270> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "TtlParseContext.blank-labels mutates in place despite immutable-style threading" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/8ef105c2-45fa-4729-912b-29a9ab655270> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/8ef105c2-45fa-4729-912b-29a9ab655270> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "The new-label branch of parse-blank-node's `_:label` handling calls `(list-push (. ctx blank-labels) (record-new BlankLabelBinding (label label-str) (id (. gen id))))` directly against the incoming context's existing list, then rebuilds the surrounding TtlParseContext with `(blank-labels (. ctx blank-labels))` — the SAME list reference, already mutated by the push — rather than constructing a new list to carry forward. So although TtlParseContext's other fields (prefixes, base-iri, state, blank-counter) are threaded in the immutable record-new style (a fresh record built and returned each time), the `blank-labels` field is a genuinely mutable, shared-reference `List` where `list-push` has a visible side effect on every alias of that list, including ones held by earlier/sibling contexts that copied the same reference.\n\nEvidence: src/parse/ttl.slop, parse-blank-node's `_:label` `(none)` arm: `(let ((gen (context-gen-blank-id arena ctx))) (do (list-push (. ctx blank-labels) (record-new BlankLabelBinding ...)) (ok (record-new TermTriplesResult ... (ctx (record-new TtlParseContext ... (blank-labels (. ctx blank-labels)) ...))))))` — no new list is allocated; the field is simply copied by reference after being mutated in place." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/8ef105c2-45fa-4729-912b-29a9ab655270> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "superseded" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/8ef105c2-45fa-4729-912b-29a9ab655270> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-02-12T06:37:10Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/8ef105c2-45fa-4729-912b-29a9ab655270> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "TtlParseContext.blank-labels mutates in place despite immutable-style threading" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/8ef105c2-45fa-4729-912b-29a9ab655270> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#learnedFrom> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/58d69b61-cacd-42a4-bf3c-5b616d359864> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/a95a78da-6580-48dc-8b92-946c33d2d64a> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Lesson> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/a95a78da-6580-48dc-8b92-946c33d2d64a> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "N3-to-RDF flattening collapses quick-vars and reuses formula ids as blank node ids" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/a95a78da-6580-48dc-8b92-946c33d2d64a> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/a95a78da-6580-48dc-8b92-946c33d2d64a> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "n3-to-rdf-graph (src/parse/n3.slop) converts every `n3-quick-var` term to `(make-blank arena 0)` regardless of the QuickVar's own name, so two distinct N3 quick variables (e.g. `?x` and `?y`) both become the identical blank node `_:b0` once an N3Graph is flattened to a plain rdf.slop Graph. The same function also casts a Formula's `id` directly to `BlankNodeId` via `(make-blank arena (cast BlankNodeId (. f id)))` — formula ids come from N3ParseContext's own `formula-counter`, a namespace that starts at 0 independently of TtlParseContext's `blank-counter`, so a parsed formula and an ordinary parsed blank node from the same document can collide on the same blank node id after conversion. Evidence: src/parse/n3.slop, `n3-to-rdf-graph`'s three `match` arms over subject/predicate/object, each mapping `(n3-quick-var qv)` to `(make-blank arena 0)` and `(n3-formula f)` to `(make-blank arena (cast BlankNodeId (. f id)))`." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/a95a78da-6580-48dc-8b92-946c33d2d64a> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/a95a78da-6580-48dc-8b92-946c33d2d64a> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-02-02T07:23:10Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/a95a78da-6580-48dc-8b92-946c33d2d64a> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "N3-to-RDF flattening collapses quick-vars and reuses formula ids as blank node ids" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/a95a78da-6580-48dc-8b92-946c33d2d64a> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#learnedFrom> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/98f6df58-7ca4-432e-8809-4e28875d5002> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/bb5464fa-82cf-4663-b6a1-877f9409c8f6> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Lesson> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/bb5464fa-82cf-4663-b6a1-877f9409c8f6> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "slop tester @example precondition check has two upstream bugs; fix in slop, not slop-rdf" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/bb5464fa-82cf-4663-b6a1-877f9409c8f6> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/bb5464fa-82cf-4663-b6a1-877f9409c8f6> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Since slop commit 5171819 (2026-08-20, in 0.2.1/0.2.2) `slop test` emits a precondition check before every @example call. Two defects live in lib/compiler/tester/test-emit.slop and must be fixed there, not worked around in slop-rdf: (1) bind-precondition-args / substitute-symbol substitute example arguments for parameter names symbol-by-symbol, so a dot-shorthand `ctx.state` in a @pre is one symbol that never matches param `ctx` and is emitted as the undeclared C identifier `ctx_state`; the same @pre expands correctly in the function's own SLOP_PRE. (2) build-precondition-check transpiles the substituted condition with plain transpile-expr, so `_` wildcards in example arguments (which the call itself renders as a zero initializer via transpile-expr-safe) fail with \"unknown symbol '_'\" and the test is reported unrunnable. Observed 2026-09-11 when slop-rdf moved from a June-2026 slop to 0.2.2: ttl.slop, n3.slop, serialize-ttl.slop and serialize-n3.slop failed to compile under `slop test`; 113 tests pass once @pre uses `(. x f)` and example args are concrete, which confirms the diagnosis but is not the accepted fix. Separately, two slop-rdf examples are genuinely malformed and need fixing in slop-rdf regardless: parse-path-expression in n3.slop uses `...` inside an argument (the tester deliberately reports \"'...' is not a value\"), and parse-triple in ttl.slop passes a bare undefined symbol `prefixes`." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/bb5464fa-82cf-4663-b6a1-877f9409c8f6> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/bb5464fa-82cf-4663-b6a1-877f9409c8f6> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasRationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/91bc50a0-06d2-4e89-8ee2-f3450a7af0a8> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/bb5464fa-82cf-4663-b6a1-877f9409c8f6> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-09-12T00:18:11.103096Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/bb5464fa-82cf-4663-b6a1-877f9409c8f6> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "slop tester @example precondition check has two upstream bugs; fix in slop, not slop-rdf" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/bb5464fa-82cf-4663-b6a1-877f9409c8f6> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#supersedes> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/d5064f64-0e1e-4922-90ba-e39c926f2b81> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/c1cfacbe-1298-44fa-bc27-7e98528a786b> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Lesson> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/c1cfacbe-1298-44fa-bc27-7e98528a786b> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Duplicate @assume beside an unremoved serialize-literal postcondition" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/c1cfacbe-1298-44fa-bc27-7e98528a786b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/c1cfacbe-1298-44fa-bc27-7e98528a786b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "serialize-literal's pre-existing `(@post (> (string-len $result) 0))` (src/serialize/serialize-ttl.slop) gets a same-predicate `(@assume (> (string-len $result) 0))` inserted directly beneath it, with the `@post` left in place rather than replaced. Elsewhere in this codebase `@assume` denotes a trusted axiom the verifier does not prove (e.g. IndexedGraph's SPO/PSO/OSP query-correctness axioms), so pairing one with an already-declared `@post` on the identical predicate reads as a signal that the verifier could not statically discharge that `@post` for serialize-literal, and the assumption was added so the property could still be relied on. Because the `@post` was not removed, it's unclear from the diff alone whether it is still runtime-checked or now redundant with the new axiom — the commit message (\"verifier fixes\", no body) does not say. Evidence: src/serialize/serialize-ttl.slop, the `+(@assume (> (string-len $result) 0))` line inserted immediately after serialize-literal's `(@post (> (string-len $result) 0))`." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/c1cfacbe-1298-44fa-bc27-7e98528a786b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/c1cfacbe-1298-44fa-bc27-7e98528a786b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-02-17T19:28:51Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/c1cfacbe-1298-44fa-bc27-7e98528a786b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Duplicate @assume beside an unremoved serialize-literal postcondition" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/d5064f64-0e1e-4922-90ba-e39c926f2b81> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Lesson> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/d5064f64-0e1e-4922-90ba-e39c926f2b81> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "slop tester @example precondition check needs explicit field access and concrete args" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/d5064f64-0e1e-4922-90ba-e39c926f2b81> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/d5064f64-0e1e-4922-90ba-e39c926f2b81> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "On functions that carry both @pre and @example, write the @pre with explicit `(. x f)` field access (never `x.f` dot-shorthand) and give the @example fully concrete argument values (never `_` or `...` wildcards in argument position). Why: since slop commit 5171819 (\"issue #71 - slop test problems\", 2026-08-20, shipped in 0.2.1/0.2.2) `slop test` emits a precondition check before every @example call, built by bind-precondition-args in lib/compiler/tester/test-emit.slop. It substitutes example arguments for parameter names symbol-by-symbol and transpiles the result with the plain transpiler, so (a) `ctx.state` is a single symbol that never matches param `ctx` and is mangled to the undeclared C identifier `ctx_state`, and (b) `_` wildcards in arguments hit \"unknown symbol '_'\" and the test is reported unrunnable. Both are tester bugs rather than a language tightening: the same `ctx.state` still expands correctly in the function's own SLOP_PRE, and the call itself renders `_` as a zero initializer via transpile-expr-safe. Evidence: upgrading slop-rdf from a June-2026 slop to 0.2.2 on 2026-09-11 made 4 of 7 test files fail to compile (ttl.slop, n3.slop, serialize-ttl.slop, serialize-n3.slop); rewriting 11 @pre sites to `(. x f)` and ~20 example argument tuples to concrete `(PrefixMap (list PrefixBinding) 0) (none) (list BlankLabelBinding) 0` restored all 113 tests. Wildcards in the EXPECTED value remain fine. Constraint lapses if the upstream tester substitutes dotted symbols and applies replace-wildcards to arguments." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/d5064f64-0e1e-4922-90ba-e39c926f2b81> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "superseded" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/d5064f64-0e1e-4922-90ba-e39c926f2b81> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-09-12T00:16:49.825857Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/d5064f64-0e1e-4922-90ba-e39c926f2b81> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "slop tester @example precondition check needs explicit field access and concrete args" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/d5064f64-0e1e-4922-90ba-e39c926f2b81> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#isSupersededBy> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/bb5464fa-82cf-4663-b6a1-877f9409c8f6> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/f7527654-75a3-45bd-908d-4b4c45ac24f9> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Lesson> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/f7527654-75a3-45bd-908d-4b4c45ac24f9> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "xsd-compare ignores literal language tags" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/f7527654-75a3-45bd-908d-4b4c45ac24f9> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/f7527654-75a3-45bd-908d-4b4c45ac24f9> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "xsd-compare (src/xsd.slop) determines each operand's XSD type solely from `(. lit-a datatype)` / `(. lit-b datatype)` (defaulting a missing datatype to XSD_STRING) and never inspects `(. lit-a lang)` / `(. lit-b lang)` at all, so two language-tagged literals with the same lexical value but different language tags (e.g. \"chat\"@en vs \"chat\"@fr) compare as xsd-compare-equal. This diverges from the existing literal-values-equal, whose first match arm explicitly branches on `(. a lang)` / `(. b lang)` and only treats two literals as equal when both carry a language tag and the tags match. Evidence: src/xsd.slop's new xsd-compare body (`(let ((dt-a (match (. lit-a datatype) ((some d) d) ((none) XSD_STRING))) ...) ...)`, no lang lookup) versus the pre-existing literal-values-equal's `(match (. a lang) ((some lang-a) (match (. b lang) ((some lang-b) (if (string-eq lang-a lang-b) ...)) ((none) (ok false)))) ((none) ...))` structure." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/f7527654-75a3-45bd-908d-4b4c45ac24f9> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/f7527654-75a3-45bd-908d-4b4c45ac24f9> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-02-11T19:37:39Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/f7527654-75a3-45bd-908d-4b4c45ac24f9> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "xsd-compare ignores literal language tags" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/f7527654-75a3-45bd-908d-4b4c45ac24f9> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#learnedFrom> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/2512c82a-b606-4fea-9047-acb6b5157799> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/3e715e8a-d448-4b32-85a3-9ac51568c607> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Pattern> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/3e715e8a-d448-4b32-85a3-9ac51568c607> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "RDF terms as closed 3-way union" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/3e715e8a-d448-4b32-85a3-9ac51568c607> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/3e715e8a-d448-4b32-85a3-9ac51568c607> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Term is modeled as a closed tagged union of exactly `(iri IRI) | (blank BlankNode) | (literal Literal)`, dispatched via exhaustive `match` rather than open subtyping/interfaces. Evidence: src/rdf.slop, `(type Term (union (iri IRI) (blank BlankNode) (literal Literal)))`, with term-kind/term-eq/literal-eq all implemented as exhaustive match arms over the three variants. Mirrors RDF 1.1's fixed set of term kinds." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/3e715e8a-d448-4b32-85a3-9ac51568c607> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "superseded" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/3e715e8a-d448-4b32-85a3-9ac51568c607> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-01-20T17:26:41Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/3e715e8a-d448-4b32-85a3-9ac51568c607> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "RDF terms as closed 3-way union" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/59ad5b6e-e8a3-4ecd-8d3e-9d643528801c> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Pattern> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/59ad5b6e-e8a3-4ecd-8d3e-9d643528801c> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Inductive loop-invariant annotations for accumulator postconditions" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/59ad5b6e-e8a3-4ecd-8d3e-9d643528801c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/59ad5b6e-e8a3-4ecd-8d3e-9d643528801c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Adding an explicit `@loop-invariant` inside a `for-each` loop that mutates an accumulator lets the contract verifier inductively prove the enclosing function's `@post` about that accumulator, instead of the postcondition being unprovable across the loop body. Evidence: src/serialize/serialize-n3.slop's `serialize-formula` gets `(@loop-invariant (starts-with result \"{\"))` inside the `for-each` that repeatedly `string-concat`s onto the mutable `result` string, supporting its pre-existing `(@post (starts-with $result \"{\"))`. src/serialize/serialize-ttl.slop's `serialize-iri` gets `(@loop-invariant (match compressed ((some s) (> (string-len s) 0)) ((none) true)))` inside the `for-each` over prefix bindings, supporting its pre-existing `(@post (> (string-len $result) 0))` which is established via the final `match` on `compressed` after the loop." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/59ad5b6e-e8a3-4ecd-8d3e-9d643528801c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/59ad5b6e-e8a3-4ecd-8d3e-9d643528801c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-02-17T19:28:51Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/59ad5b6e-e8a3-4ecd-8d3e-9d643528801c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Inductive loop-invariant annotations for accumulator postconditions" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/5d9eda86-0fce-4e0f-b767-cf5a13aea5fd> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Pattern> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/5d9eda86-0fce-4e0f-b767-cf5a13aea5fd> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Immutable ParseState threading for hand-rolled RDF parsers" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/5d9eda86-0fce-4e0f-b767-cf5a13aea5fd> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/5d9eda86-0fce-4e0f-b767-cf5a13aea5fd> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Turtle and N3 parsing share a new common.slop module built around an immutable ParseState/Position record threaded functionally through every parse function — state-advance, skip-whitespace, skip-line, parse-while, parse-until, expect-char each take a ParseState and return a new one (or a Result wrapping one) rather than mutating parser state in place. Evidence: src/parse/common.slop (new, 213 lines) — `(type ParseState (record (input String) (offset (Int 0 ..)) (line (Int 1 ..)) (column (Int 1 ..))))`; `state-advance` builds a fresh `record-new ParseState` bumping `line`/resetting `column` on newline (char code 10) instead of assigning into an existing struct. ttl.slop and n3.slop both build on this same primitive (TtlParseContext wraps a ParseState; N3ParseContext wraps a TtlParseContext) rather than each defining their own char-stream mechanism. Consequence: with no record-update/spread syntax available, every ttl.slop/n3.slop function that advances state must manually re-list every field of TtlParseContext/N3ParseContext even when only one field changed — producing dozens of near-identical multi-line record-new blocks throughout both files." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/5d9eda86-0fce-4e0f-b767-cf5a13aea5fd> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/5d9eda86-0fce-4e0f-b767-cf5a13aea5fd> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-02-02T07:23:10Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/5d9eda86-0fce-4e0f-b767-cf5a13aea5fd> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Immutable ParseState threading for hand-rolled RDF parsers" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/947c321d-754a-4763-aaaa-ee2fc1b2b112> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Pattern> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/947c321d-754a-4763-aaaa-ee2fc1b2b112> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Tiered LLM routing for hole-filling" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/947c321d-754a-4763-aaaa-ee2fc1b2b112> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/947c321d-754a-4763-aaaa-ee2fc1b2b112> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Slop code-generation holes are routed to different LLM tiers by complexity, configured in slop.toml: tier-1 (booleans/arithmetic/field access) and tier-2 (conditionals/Result construction/simple transforms) use Claude Haiku 4.5 / Sonnet 4.5 via OpenRouter; tier-3 (loops, multi-conditional, state manipulation) uses Sonnet 4.5 with a smaller 8192 context and temperature 0.5; tier-4 (algorithms, state machines, complex logic) uses Opus 4.5 with a 128000 context and temperature 0.6. Routing retries up to max_retries=2 and escalates to a higher tier on failure (escalate_on_failure=true). A separate \"claude-code\" interactive provider (clipboard mode) exists alongside the programmatic OpenRouter provider. Evidence: slop.toml `[tiers.tier-1..4]` and `[routing]` sections and their inline comments describing each tier's complexity band." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/947c321d-754a-4763-aaaa-ee2fc1b2b112> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/947c321d-754a-4763-aaaa-ee2fc1b2b112> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-01-20T17:26:41Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/947c321d-754a-4763-aaaa-ee2fc1b2b112> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Tiered LLM routing for hole-filling" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/9713b735-92cc-4372-b494-c801f4644403> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Pattern> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/9713b735-92cc-4372-b494-c801f4644403> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "list-push-triples / graph-add-all accumulator helpers" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/9713b735-92cc-4372-b494-c801f4644403> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/9713b735-92cc-4372-b494-c801f4644403> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "ttl.slop replaces its repeated `(for-each (t src) (list-push acc t))` / `(for-each (t src) (set! g (graph-add-unchecked arena g t)))` inline loops with two new helpers — `list-push-triples` `(Arena (List Triple) (List Triple)) -> (List Triple)` and `graph-add-all` `(Arena Graph (List Triple)) -> Graph` — and every call site now explicitly re-threads the result via `set!` (e.g. `(set! triples (list-push-triples arena triples (. er extra-triples)))`, `(set! g (graph-add-all arena g (. sr extra-triples)))`) rather than assuming the passed-in accumulator was mutated in place and left unread.\n\nWhy: consolidates duplicated for-each/list-push and for-each/graph-add-unchecked loops across parse-triple-term, parse-collection-adjacent code, parse-predicate-object-list, parse-object-list, parse-reified-triple, and parse-ttl-string's main loop into two named, spec'd helpers, cutting repetition while making every call site capture and reassign the accumulator explicitly instead of relying on an implicit in-place mutation to be visible to the caller.\n\nEvidence: commit 937461fe5b, src/parse/ttl.slop new `(fn list-push-triples ...)` (@intent \"Append every triple from src onto dst, returning the combined list\") and `(fn graph-add-all ...)` (@intent \"Add every triple from src to the graph, returning the new graph\"), plus their ~7 call sites each replacing an inline `for-each` loop with a `set!`-assigned call to one of the helpers." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/9713b735-92cc-4372-b494-c801f4644403> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/9713b735-92cc-4372-b494-c801f4644403> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-06-26T02:06:40Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/9713b735-92cc-4372-b494-c801f4644403> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "list-push-triples / graph-add-all accumulator helpers" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/d34efb38-e03c-4503-b951-36925eb2991f> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Pattern> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/d34efb38-e03c-4503-b951-36925eb2991f> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "RDF terms as closed 4-way union with triple terms" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/d34efb38-e03c-4503-b951-36925eb2991f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/d34efb38-e03c-4503-b951-36925eb2991f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Term is now a 4-way tagged union — `(type Term (union (term-iri IRI) (term-blank BlankNode) (term-literal Literal) (term-triple (Ptr Triple))))` — up from the previously-closed 3-way union of exactly iri/blank/literal. `TermKind` gains a matching `triple` enum case, and every exhaustive match over Term (term-kind, term-eq, term-free) gains a `(term-triple ...)` arm; term-eq's recurses into `triple-eq` on the two wrapped triples, so term equality can now recurse through arbitrarily nested triple terms (a term-triple's own subject/predicate/object may themselves be term-triple values — nothing in the type bounds nesting depth). A new `make-triple-term(arena, Triple) -> Term` constructor arena-allocates the wrapped Triple behind the Ptr. Evidence: src/rdf.slop diff — the `Term` union and `TermKind` enum changes, `make-triple-term`'s `(@post (match $result ((term-triple _) true) (_ false)))`, and the added match arms in term-kind/term-eq/term-free." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/d34efb38-e03c-4503-b951-36925eb2991f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/d34efb38-e03c-4503-b951-36925eb2991f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasRationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/9444a980-8d31-4423-918b-0c73bfec223d> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/d34efb38-e03c-4503-b951-36925eb2991f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-06-25T20:02:50Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/d34efb38-e03c-4503-b951-36925eb2991f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "RDF terms as closed 4-way union with triple terms" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/d34efb38-e03c-4503-b951-36925eb2991f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#supersedes> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/3e715e8a-d448-4b32-85a3-9ac51568c607> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/e8127683-72b3-4401-bad4-eb945bf3d074> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Pattern> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/e8127683-72b3-4401-bad4-eb945bf3d074> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "ctx-with-state + (?) threading to cut TtlParseContext boilerplate" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/e8127683-72b3-4401-bad4-eb945bf3d074> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/e8127683-72b3-4401-bad4-eb945bf3d074> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "ttl.slop's parse functions replace nested `(match r ((ok x) ...) ((error e) (error e)))` error-propagation chains and repeated multi-field `(record-new TtlParseContext (prefixes ...) (base-iri ...) (blank-labels ...) (blank-counter ...) (state ...))` blocks with the `(? expr)` result-unwrapping form plus a single new `ctx-with-state` helper that copies every TtlParseContext field but `state` in one place: `(fn ctx-with-state ((in ctx TtlParseContext) (in state ParseState)) (record-new TtlParseContext (prefixes (. ctx prefixes)) (base-iri (. ctx base-iri)) (blank-labels (. ctx blank-labels)) (blank-counter (. ctx blank-counter)) (state state)))`. Dozens of call sites across parse-iri-ref, parse-prefixed-name, parse-term-extended, parse-predicate-object-list, parse-object-list, parse-directive, and parse-ttl-string are rewritten this way in the same commit, directly cutting the per-call-site full-field-listing boilerplate previously flagged as a consequence of the \"Immutable ParseState threading\" pattern. This same threading style is what makes the commit's new multi-step parse-triple-term and parse-annotation functions (each chaining several fallible sub-parses) tractable to write flatly. Evidence: commit b48ba5c diff across src/parse/ttl.slop — e.g. parse-iri-ref's `(let ((res (? (parse-until arena s1 62)))) (ok (record-new TermResult (term ...) (ctx (ctx-with-state ctx (. res state))))))` replacing its prior nested match; parse-object-list's inner loop body switching to `(let ((s1 ...) (objr (? (parse-term-extended ...)))) (do ...))`." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/e8127683-72b3-4401-bad4-eb945bf3d074> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/e8127683-72b3-4401-bad4-eb945bf3d074> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-06-25T20:02:50Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/e8127683-72b3-4401-bad4-eb945bf3d074> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "ctx-with-state + (?) threading to cut TtlParseContext boilerplate" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/115318b7-88ab-4895-83c3-b074fca4e09f> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/115318b7-88ab-4895-83c3-b074fca4e09f> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: indexed-graph-for-each diverges from indexed-graph-match's linear scan" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/115318b7-88ab-4895-83c3-b074fca4e09f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/115318b7-88ab-4895-83c3-b074fca4e09f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "This commit gives indexed-graph-for-each its own SPO/PSO/OSP index-dispatch implementation, so its filtering logic is no longer duplicated verbatim with indexed-graph-match (which is untouched by this commit and still linear-scans g.triples). Evidence: src/index.slop — indexed-graph-for-each's single `(for-each (t (. g triples)) ...)` scan with inline subj/pred/obj matching was replaced by nested `(match subj ((some s) (match (map-get (. (. g index) spo) s) ...)) ((none) (match pred ...)))` dispatch through the spo/pso/osp maps, and its @intent changed from \"Call callback for each matching triple - zero allocation\" to \"Call callback for each matching triple using indices - zero allocation\"." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/115318b7-88ab-4895-83c3-b074fca4e09f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/115318b7-88ab-4895-83c3-b074fca4e09f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-02-05T18:00:36Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/115318b7-88ab-4895-83c3-b074fca4e09f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: indexed-graph-for-each diverges from indexed-graph-match's linear scan" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/22018cfd-d2a0-4ea3-a8b2-e96da982bef7> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/22018cfd-d2a0-4ea3-a8b2-e96da982bef7> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "later-decision" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/22018cfd-d2a0-4ea3-a8b2-e96da982bef7> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: Blank label map for `_:label` node identity" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/22018cfd-d2a0-4ea3-a8b2-e96da982bef7> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/22018cfd-d2a0-4ea3-a8b2-e96da982bef7> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "The linear blank-label-lookup made label-heavy files quadratic, and the List had to be threaded back through the ctx by hand (Lesson 6ae8639d). A Map is a pointer, so inserts are visible without rethreading, and lookup is O(1). Storing the table's arena alongside the map is what lets the streaming parse keep labels long-lived while everything else in a statement goes to scratch (see \"Per-statement scratch arena for streaming TTL parse\")." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/22018cfd-d2a0-4ea3-a8b2-e96da982bef7> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/22018cfd-d2a0-4ea3-a8b2-e96da982bef7> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-09-30T04:14:05.370136Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/22018cfd-d2a0-4ea3-a8b2-e96da982bef7> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: Blank label map for `_:label` node identity" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/452e3824-a019-4ba3-b0bc-6a3547efac1f> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/452e3824-a019-4ba3-b0bc-6a3547efac1f> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: Restore term-eq result postcondition" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/452e3824-a019-4ba3-b0bc-6a3547efac1f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/452e3824-a019-4ba3-b0bc-6a3547efac1f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "term-eq's `(@post (== $result (== a b)))` — removed for performance in the 2026-02-05 \"Postcondition pruning in indexed-graph-add and term-eq\" decision — is re-added verbatim by this \"verifier fixes\" commit (no commit body given). The diff restores exactly the deleted assertion with the @example lines otherwise unchanged, so the correctness/verifier coverage this postcondition gave up was apparently judged worth reinstating the per-call runtime-check cost. This is only a partial reversal: indexed-graph-add's paired postcondition removal (`(@post (indexed-graph-contains $result t))` in src/index.slop) is untouched by this commit and remains pruned." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/452e3824-a019-4ba3-b0bc-6a3547efac1f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/452e3824-a019-4ba3-b0bc-6a3547efac1f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-02-17T19:28:51Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/452e3824-a019-4ba3-b0bc-6a3547efac1f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: Restore term-eq result postcondition" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/53994bb8-7fab-4d6f-8163-e825cc46f579> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/53994bb8-7fab-4d6f-8163-e825cc46f579> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: SPO/PSO/OSP dispatch restored in indexed-graph-match" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/53994bb8-7fab-4d6f-8163-e825cc46f579> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/53994bb8-7fab-4d6f-8163-e825cc46f579> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "The prior linear-scan decision traded away O(1) index lookup specifically to avoid allocating a fresh Triple per query. That trade-off is now moot: the later \"Triple-valued leaves in TripleIndex\" decision made SPO/PSO/OSP index leaves store full Triple references (TripleSet) instead of bare terms, so an index-dispatched lookup can push the same stored triple into the result list with zero allocation — the same reasoning indexed-graph-for-each already used when it regained index dispatch. Evidence: commit 35d7d2491614fd188c2e4c6eae2c583cde5cdc1f, src/index.slop — indexed-graph-match's lookups (e.g. `(map-get (. (. g index) spo) s)` then `(map-get pred-map p)`) resolve to a triple-set whose members are pushed via `(list-push result t)` with `t` drawn straight from the index leaf, not reconstructed." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/53994bb8-7fab-4d6f-8163-e825cc46f579> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/53994bb8-7fab-4d6f-8163-e825cc46f579> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-02-06T18:30:48Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/53994bb8-7fab-4d6f-8163-e825cc46f579> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: SPO/PSO/OSP dispatch restored in indexed-graph-match" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/58d5f796-1949-4984-b98b-56a6db65bd42> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/58d5f796-1949-4984-b98b-56a6db65bd42> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: Linear-scan filtering replaces index dispatch in indexed-graph-match" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/58d5f796-1949-4984-b98b-56a6db65bd42> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/58d5f796-1949-4984-b98b-56a6db65bd42> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "To return matched triples without allocating fresh Triple objects per query, indexed-graph-match abandons its SPO/PSO/OSP index dispatch in favor of an unconditional linear scan over g.triples with per-field equality filtering, trading the index's O(1)-average lookup for zero per-query allocation. Evidence: src/index.slop — indexed-graph-match's @intent changed from \"Find all triples matching pattern using optimal index\" to \"Find all triples matching pattern - returns existing triples without allocation\", and its ~80-line nested subj/pred/obj index-dispatch block was deleted and replaced by a single for-each loop, under new comments \"Simple filtering approach - iterate existing triples, no allocation of new Triple objects\" and \"Trade O(1) index lookup for zero memory allocation per query\"." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/58d5f796-1949-4984-b98b-56a6db65bd42> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/58d5f796-1949-4984-b98b-56a6db65bd42> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-02-04T23:47:59Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/58d5f796-1949-4984-b98b-56a6db65bd42> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: Linear-scan filtering replaces index dispatch in indexed-graph-match" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/91bc50a0-06d2-4e89-8ee2-f3450a7af0a8> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/91bc50a0-06d2-4e89-8ee2-f3450a7af0a8> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "record-was-inaccurate" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/91bc50a0-06d2-4e89-8ee2-f3450a7af0a8> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: slop tester @example precondition check has two upstream bugs; fix in slop, not slop-rdf" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/91bc50a0-06d2-4e89-8ee2-f3450a7af0a8> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/91bc50a0-06d2-4e89-8ee2-f3450a7af0a8> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "The first record framed rewriting slop-rdf contracts and examples as the fix. The maintainer rejected that: slop-rdf must not work around slop bugs, so the record was inaccurate about where the fix belongs. The replacement pins the defects to the tester and separates them from the two genuinely malformed slop-rdf examples." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/91bc50a0-06d2-4e89-8ee2-f3450a7af0a8> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/91bc50a0-06d2-4e89-8ee2-f3450a7af0a8> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-09-12T00:18:11.103096Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/91bc50a0-06d2-4e89-8ee2-f3450a7af0a8> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: slop tester @example precondition check has two upstream bugs; fix in slop, not slop-rdf" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/9444a980-8d31-4423-918b-0c73bfec223d> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/9444a980-8d31-4423-918b-0c73bfec223d> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: RDF terms as closed 4-way union with triple terms" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/9444a980-8d31-4423-918b-0c73bfec223d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/9444a980-8d31-4423-918b-0c73bfec223d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "RDF 1.2 introduces triple terms — first-class RDF terms wrapping an embedded (subject, predicate, object) triple — used both directly as an object via `<<( s p o )>>` Turtle syntax and as the object of the generated `rdf:reifies` triple that backs `{| ... |}` annotation-block reification. The previously-closed 3-way Term union (iri | blank | literal) structurally could not represent this, so it gains a fourth variant rather than staying closed. Evidence: commit b48ba5c (merged via PR #3 \"rdf12-fixes\"), src/rdf.slop." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/9444a980-8d31-4423-918b-0c73bfec223d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/9444a980-8d31-4423-918b-0c73bfec223d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-06-25T20:02:50Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/9444a980-8d31-4423-918b-0c73bfec223d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: RDF terms as closed 4-way union with triple terms" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/a2b3f37d-d22d-4a2c-b6a0-896bee5d9a2f> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/a2b3f37d-d22d-4a2c-b6a0-896bee5d9a2f> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: contains/subjects/objects revert to direct term-level set operations" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/a2b3f37d-d22d-4a2c-b6a0-896bee5d9a2f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/a2b3f37d-d22d-4a2c-b6a0-896bee5d9a2f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Now that leaves store bare Term again, indexed-graph-contains/subjects/objects no longer need whole-Triple membership/extraction logic and go back to simpler direct Set-Term operations. Evidence: src/index.slop — indexed-graph-subjects replaces its for-each-with-found-flag scan of a triple-set (checking `(term-eq (triple-predicate t) pred)` per triple) with a direct `(when (set-has pred-set pred) (list-push result s))`; indexed-graph-objects replaces `(for-each (t triple-set) (list-push result (triple-object t)))` with `(for-each (o obj-set) (list-push result o))`." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/a2b3f37d-d22d-4a2c-b6a0-896bee5d9a2f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/a2b3f37d-d22d-4a2c-b6a0-896bee5d9a2f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-04-13T13:58:16Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/a2b3f37d-d22d-4a2c-b6a0-896bee5d9a2f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: contains/subjects/objects revert to direct term-level set operations" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/acfa5b30-93b2-4f92-920f-3517bdbaf2fd> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/acfa5b30-93b2-4f92-920f-3517bdbaf2fd> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: Term-valued leaves restore memory efficiency in TripleIndex" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/acfa5b30-93b2-4f92-920f-3517bdbaf2fd> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/acfa5b30-93b2-4f92-920f-3517bdbaf2fd> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Memory usage became the priority (commit message: \"memory usage improvements for IndexedGraph\"); the earlier zero-allocation lookup gained by storing full Triple at leaves is given up because the extra ~3x memory (216 vs 72 bytes/key) outweighed it. Evidence: src/index.slop, new comment above `(type TermSet (Set Term))`: \"This saves ~3x memory vs storing full Triple (72 bytes vs 216 bytes per key)\"." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/acfa5b30-93b2-4f92-920f-3517bdbaf2fd> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/acfa5b30-93b2-4f92-920f-3517bdbaf2fd> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-04-13T13:58:16Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/acfa5b30-93b2-4f92-920f-3517bdbaf2fd> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: Term-valued leaves restore memory efficiency in TripleIndex" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/ce4889b0-97fe-470f-a24e-ed4979a7f46e> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/ce4889b0-97fe-470f-a24e-ed4979a7f46e> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: blank-labels field projection drops pushes without explicit rethread" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/ce4889b0-97fe-470f-a24e-ed4979a7f46e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/ce4889b0-97fe-470f-a24e-ed4979a7f46e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "The prior Lesson's premise — that `(. ctx blank-labels)` is a shared mutable reference where `list-push` visibly mutates every alias — does not hold reliably in practice. This commit's fix (and its new coreference test) show the projected field can be a copy: pushing a new `BlankLabelBinding` onto `(. ctx blank-labels)` and then rebuilding the context via `(ctx-with-state (. gen ctx) ...)` could silently drop the binding, so `_:x` used twice risked generating two distinct blank nodes instead of coreferencing. Evidence: commit 937461fe5b0d79a33d7827b543df2010ca415c02, subject \"parsing fix for RDF12\"." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/ce4889b0-97fe-470f-a24e-ed4979a7f46e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/ce4889b0-97fe-470f-a24e-ed4979a7f46e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-06-26T02:06:40Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/ce4889b0-97fe-470f-a24e-ed4979a7f46e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: blank-labels field projection drops pushes without explicit rethread" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/ce8986a6-39f9-4f56-b671-ed8ef4e4680c> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/ce8986a6-39f9-4f56-b671-ed8ef4e4680c> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: indexed-graph-match regains index-assisted lookup" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/ce8986a6-39f9-4f56-b671-ed8ef4e4680c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/ce8986a6-39f9-4f56-b671-ed8ef4e4680c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "This directly reverses the \"indexed-graph-match becomes O(n) regardless of binding\" consequence: that commit deliberately traded O(1) lookup away because index leaves only stored bare terms at the time. Now that leaves store full Triple references (per \"Triple-valued leaves in TripleIndex\"), that trade-off no longer holds and index dispatch is restored without reintroducing per-query allocation. Evidence: commit 35d7d2491614fd188c2e4c6eae2c583cde5cdc1f, src/index.slop." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/ce8986a6-39f9-4f56-b671-ed8ef4e4680c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/ce8986a6-39f9-4f56-b671-ed8ef4e4680c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-02-06T18:30:48Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/ce8986a6-39f9-4f56-b671-ed8ef4e4680c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: indexed-graph-match regains index-assisted lookup" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/e891e3bb-1db8-4f38-9247-5798562cddf8> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/e891e3bb-1db8-4f38-9247-5798562cddf8> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: match/for-each reintroduce per-query Triple allocation via record-new" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/e891e3bb-1db8-4f38-9247-5798562cddf8> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/e891e3bb-1db8-4f38-9247-5798562cddf8> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Because leaves no longer hold a reusable Triple reference, indexed-graph-match and indexed-graph-for-each must rebuild a Triple with record-new at every leaf hit — directly reversing the earlier \"regains near-O(1) lookup without reintroducing per-query Triple allocation\" claim, which depended on leaves holding the same Triple reference already in g.triples. Evidence: src/index.slop — e.g. the S+P+O-bound arm of indexed-graph-match changes from `(for-each (t triple-set) (when (term-eq (triple-object t) o) (list-push result t)))` to `(when (set-has term-set o) (list-push result (record-new Triple (subject s) (predicate p) (object o))))`; indexed-graph-for-each's callback sites are rewritten the same way." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/e891e3bb-1db8-4f38-9247-5798562cddf8> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/e891e3bb-1db8-4f38-9247-5798562cddf8> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-04-13T13:58:16Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/e891e3bb-1db8-4f38-9247-5798562cddf8> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: match/for-each reintroduce per-query Triple allocation via record-new" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/f74d5b7e-8716-448f-bc7d-011d01c0ca30> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/f74d5b7e-8716-448f-bc7d-011d01c0ca30> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: Term-valued leaves restore term-eq-based Set/Map membership" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/f74d5b7e-8716-448f-bc7d-011d01c0ca30> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/f74d5b7e-8716-448f-bc7d-011d01c0ca30> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "The leaf element type reverted from Triple back to Term, so Set/Map membership and hashing at the index leaves goes back through a single term-eq per element instead of triple-eq (subject+predicate+object). Evidence: src/index.slop — indexed-graph-contains now does `(set-has obj-set o)` (single-Term membership) instead of `(set-has triple-set t)` (whole-Triple membership); indexed-graph-add's set-put calls now insert a bare `o` or `p` Term instead of the whole triple `t`." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/f74d5b7e-8716-448f-bc7d-011d01c0ca30> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/f74d5b7e-8716-448f-bc7d-011d01c0ca30> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-04-13T13:58:16Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/f74d5b7e-8716-448f-bc7d-011d01c0ca30> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: Term-valued leaves restore term-eq-based Set/Map membership" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/67bfd7cb-92d3-4eab-9eef-ef25be5862ed> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Requirement> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/67bfd7cb-92d3-4eab-9eef-ef25be5862ed> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Streaming TTL parse memory bounded by one statement" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/67bfd7cb-92d3-4eab-9eef-ef25be5862ed> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/67bfd7cb-92d3-4eab-9eef-ef25be5862ed> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "The streaming Turtle parse (parse-ttl-file-for-each-triple) must run in memory proportional to a statement, not the document: peak resident memory about the input file size plus a small constant, with no change to the triples delivered, their order, blank-node ids, term content, or the non-streaming parse-ttl-file / parse-ttl-string results. Driven by HOWL, which streams the GO (76 MB), EL-GALEN (7.1 MB) and OBI (5 MB) ontologies and prints blank ids in its reports, offset per imported document." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/67bfd7cb-92d3-4eab-9eef-ef25be5862ed> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/67bfd7cb-92d3-4eab-9eef-ef25be5862ed> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-09-30T04:14:41.312219Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/67bfd7cb-92d3-4eab-9eef-ef25be5862ed> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Streaming TTL parse memory bounded by one statement" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/f9a5a045-5834-4b91-84f6-77b00174148a> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Requirement> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/f9a5a045-5834-4b91-84f6-77b00174148a> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Callers' loop invariants over RDF terms must be verifiable" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/f9a5a045-5834-4b91-84f6-77b00174148a> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/f9a5a045-5834-4b91-84f6-77b00174148a> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Code built on slop-rdf (notably growl's rule loops) states @loop-invariants that construct or read Terms and Triples; SLOP's verifier (slop#228) can only check those when the slop-rdf functions they call are @pure. slop-rdf's side-effect-free API functions should therefore be marked @pure, without changing the generated C that slop-sys vendors." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/f9a5a045-5834-4b91-84f6-77b00174148a> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/f9a5a045-5834-4b91-84f6-77b00174148a> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-09-30T06:38:08.870449Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/f9a5a045-5834-4b91-84f6-77b00174148a> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Callers' loop invariants over RDF terms must be verifiable" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
